/* GARP SCR 学習目標（LO）別 練習問題（第1〜3章・全36LO×各3問）。自作。事実はIPCC・UNFCCC・BCBS・TCFD・UN等の公開一次資料で裏取り。GARP の教材本文・模擬試験・章末問題は使っていない */
const SCR_LO13_DATA = [
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.1] A news anchor says: 'This July was the hottest July on record in our city, so the claim of long-term climate change must be wrong because it will be cooler next month.' Which response best reflects the distinction between weather and climate?","h":"1か月や1日の観測は「天気」、気候は長期統計です。","c":["A single month is weather; climate is described by statistics such as averages and variability over a long period (classically 30 years), so one month cannot confirm or refute a climate trend.","A single month is climate because it is measured at a fixed location with calibrated instruments, so it is sufficient to define the climate of that city and any later month can be ignored","Weather and climate differ only in the units used to report them; both describe the state of the atmosphere over the same timescale, so a record month is itself a climate fact","Climate refers only to the day-to-day state of the atmosphere at one location, so a record-hot month is direct proof of a long-term climate trend and the anchor's claim is correct"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 短期の観測は天気、30年規模の統計が気候。1つの月の暑さ・寒さで気候の傾向は証明も否定もできない。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC用語集は、気候を「天気の平均的状態、またはより厳密には気象変数の平均と変動の統計的記述」とし、平均化期間は古典的にWMO定義の30年とする。1か月の記録は天気（および年々の変動）の範囲の出来事であり、気候の傾向は複数十年の統計で判断する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「1か月の観測=気候」とする選択肢は、観測精度と時間スケールを取り違えている。「単位の違いだけ」「日々の状態が気候」は定義が逆。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 気象庁も平年値を30年平均（現在は1991〜2020年）で定義している。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis (AR6 WG1), Annex VII Glossary, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_AnnexVII.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.1] According to the IPCC, which statement best characterizes 'climate change'?","h":"IPCCは原因を人為に限らず定義します。人為限定はUNFCCCの定義です。","c":["A change in the state of the climate, identifiable by changes in the mean and/or variability of its properties, that persists for an extended period (typically decades or longer), whether due to natural variability or human activity.","A change of climate attributed directly or indirectly to human activity that alters the composition of the global atmosphere, in addition to natural climate variability observed over comparable time periods","Any year-to-year fluctuation in global mean surface temperature relative to the previous year, regardless of how long the change persists or whether it can be distinguished from natural variability in the record","A change in the Sun's output over its roughly 11-year sunspot cycle, which is the only cause of climate change that the IPCC recognises in any of its assessment reports, whatever other drivers are studied"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> IPCCの気候変動は「原因を問わず、数十年以上続く平均・変動の変化」。人為限定はUNFCCCの定義。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCCは気候変動を、平均や変動の変化として識別でき、数十年以上続くものと定義し、自然変動か人間活動かは問わない。一方UNFCCC第1条は、地球大気の組成を変化させる人間活動に直接・間接に起因する変化と定義し、自然の気候変動（climate variability）と区別する。試験では2つの定義の差が問われる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 人為起因に限る選択肢はUNFCCCの定義。年ごとの揺らぎは変動であり、11年周期の太陽活動だけが原因とするのは誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis (AR6 WG1), Annex VII Glossary, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_AnnexVII.pdf ／ UNFCCC, United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change, 1992, Article 1. https://unfccc.int/resource/docs/convkp/conveng.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.1] Which of the following is an example of natural internal climate variability, as opposed to an externally forced change in climate?","h":"外部要因（強制力）ではなく、気候システム内部の揺らぎです。","c":["El Nino-Southern Oscillation (ENSO) events that temporarily raise or lower global mean surface temperature","The rise in atmospheric CO2 concentration caused by fossil fuel combustion and cement production since the start of the industrial era","The cooling that followed the 1991 eruption of Mount Pinatubo, which injected sulphur dioxide into the stratosphere and lowered temperature for about two years","A multi-decadal increase in the Sun's radiative output, which changes the amount of energy entering the climate system from outside"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ENSOは気候システム内部の変動。化石燃料CO2・火山噴火・太陽活動は外部強制力。<br><br><b>解説</b> 内部変動（internal variability）は、外部強制力がなくても気候システム内部の相互作用で生じる変動で、ENSOが代表例。火山噴火や太陽放射の変化は自然起源だが外部強制力であり、化石燃料由来のCO2は人為的な外部強制力。AR6は、単年の内部変動による世界平均気温の振れを約±0.25°C（5〜95%範囲）と見積もる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ピナツボ噴火は自然だが外部（火山）強制力。「自然=内部変動」とは限らない点が罠。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis (AR6 WG1), Annex VII Glossary, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_AnnexVII.pdf ／ IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.2] According to IPCC AR6 WG1 (2021), by approximately how much did global mean sea level rise between 1901 and 2018?","h":"約20cmです。上昇速度も加速しています。","c":["About 0.20 m (likely range 0.15 to 0.25 m)","About 0.02 m (likely range 0.01 to 0.03 m)","About 0.60 m (likely range 0.50 to 0.70 m)","About 1.50 m (likely range 1.30 to 1.70 m)"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 1901〜2018年に約0.20 m上昇。速度は1.3→1.9→3.7 mm/年と加速している。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.7は、世界平均海面水位が1901〜2018年に0.20 [0.15〜0.25] m上昇したと評価する。平均上昇速度は1901〜1971年に1.3 mm/年、1971〜2006年に1.9 mm/年、2006〜2018年に3.7 mm/年と加速している。海面水位は温暖化の複数の独立した証拠の1つ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 0.02 mは小さすぎ、0.6 m・1.5 mは将来予測や極端な値で観測値ではない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.2] The IPCC AR6 WG1 assessment of observed warming reports that global surface temperature in 2011-2020 was higher than in 1850-1900 by approximately:","h":"産業革命前比で約1.1°C。陸は海より大きく上がっています。","c":["1.09°C (very likely range 0.95 to 1.20°C)","0.45°C (very likely range 0.35 to 0.55°C)","1.90°C (very likely range 1.70 to 2.10°C)","2.60°C (very likely range 2.30 to 2.90°C)"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2011〜2020年の世界平均気温は1850〜1900年より約1.09°C高い。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.2は、2011〜2020年の世界平均気温が1850〜1900年より1.09 [0.95〜1.20]°C高く、陸域（1.59°C）が海洋（0.88°C）より大きく上昇したと述べる。複数の独立した観測データセットが一致していることが、気温上昇の証拠の信頼性を支える。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1.9°Cや2.6°Cは将来シナリオ上の値と混同しやすい。0.45°Cは過小。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.2] Which statement about where the excess heat in the climate system has accumulated is supported by the observational evidence assessed in IPCC AR6 WG1?","h":"余った熱の大部分は海洋に入っています。","c":["The atmosphere absorbed most of the excess heat, with the ocean absorbing less than 10% because water has a lower heat capacity than air at the same temperature and depth","Land warming and ice loss together absorbed about half of the excess heat, while the ocean and the atmosphere shared the other half in roughly equal proportions during 1971-2018","Most excess heat has been stored in the deep solid Earth rather than in the ocean, as conduction through rock carries the surface heat down faster than ocean circulation does","Ocean warming accounted for about 91% of the heating of the climate system (1971-2018), with land, ice and the atmosphere accounting for the remainder."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候システムの加熱の約91%は海洋が吸収している（1971〜2018年）。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.2/A.4.2は、気候システムの加熱（エネルギー不均衡）のうち海洋の昇温が91%、陸域約5%、氷の損失約3%、大気約1%を占めると評価する。大気の気温だけでなく海洋熱含量や海面水位も気候変動の証拠として用いられる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 大気が主な蓄熱先とする選択肢が最も典型的な誤解。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.3] Which natural mechanism is considered the pacemaker of the glacial-interglacial cycles of the past roughly 800,000 years?","h":"地球の軌道要素の周期的な変化です。","c":["The roughly 11-year sunspot cycle, which changes total solar output by enough to start and end ice ages, together with the 22-year magnetic reversal of the Sun's polarity","Greenhouse gas emissions from early agricultural societies, which triggered each glacial period by raising CO2 and methane concentrations long before the industrial era began","Slow, predictable changes in Earth's orbital parameters (eccentricity, obliquity and precession), which alter the latitudinal and seasonal distribution of incoming sunlight","Large volcanic eruptions occurring at regular intervals of about 100,000 years, whose sulphate aerosols cooled the planet enough to build up continental ice sheets for tens of thousands of years"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 氷期・間氷期サイクルのペースメーカーは軌道要素の変化（ミランコビッチ・サイクル）。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC用語集の「軌道強制力（orbital forcing）」は、離心率・地軸傾斜・歳差という軌道要素の遅く予測可能な変化が、日射の緯度・季節分布に与える影響と説明される。この日射分布の変化がCO2など炭素循環のフィードバックを通じて増幅され、氷期・間氷期サイクルを生む。非人為的な長期の気候変動の代表的なメカニズム。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 11年周期の太陽活動は全体の放射量の変化が小さく、氷期サイクルの原動力ではない。初期農耕の影響は約8,000年前以降の話で時間軸が合わない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis (AR6 WG1), Annex VII Glossary, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_AnnexVII.pdf ／ 用語集 Orbital forcing の項"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.3] Which statement correctly relates ice-core records (which extend back about 800,000 years) to present-day CO2 levels?","h":"氷床コアの気泡は過去の大気の直接サンプルです。","c":["Ice-core CO2 reached today's levels (above 400 ppm) in several earlier interglacials, so the present level is within the natural range seen over the past 800,000 years","Ice-core CO2 stayed roughly within 180-300 ppm over the glacial-interglacial cycles, and 2019 concentrations were higher than at any time in at least 2 million years.","Ice-core CO2 was roughly constant at about 280 ppm throughout the past 800,000 years, with no glacial-interglacial variation visible in the record","Ice cores record only past temperature (from isotopes) and cannot provide any information on past greenhouse gas concentrations in the atmosphere"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 氷床コアの気泡からCO2が分かり、2019年の濃度は少なくとも200万年で最高。<br><br><b>解説</b> 氷床コアに閉じ込められた気泡は過去の大気の直接サンプルで、CO2は氷期・間氷期サイクルで約180〜300 ppmの範囲を変動した。AR6 WG1 SPM A.2.1は、2019年のCO2濃度が少なくとも200万年で最も高く（高信頼度）、CH4とN2Oは少なくとも80万年で最も高いとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「現在の濃度は自然範囲内」は誤り。「約280 ppmで一定」は産業革命前の値で、氷期には約180 ppmまで下がった。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.3] Which pairing of a paleoclimate archive and what it records is correct?","h":"氷床コアは大気そのものを閉じ込めています。","c":["Tree rings: air samples of past atmospheric composition back to 800,000 years","Marine sediment foraminifera shells: annual snowfall accumulation","Ice-core air bubbles: direct samples of past atmospheric composition, including CO2 and CH4","Pollen records: past atmospheric CO2 measured directly from trapped air"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 氷床コアの気泡は過去の温室効果ガス濃度を直接示す。年輪は成長条件、有孔虫殻は海水の同位体を示す。<br><br><b>解説</b> プロキシ（間接指標）ごとに記録する内容が異なる。氷床コアの気泡は過去の大気組成を直接保存する。年輪は気温・水分などの成長条件を年単位で数百〜数千年遡って記録し、海底堆積物中の有孔虫殻の酸素同位体は海水温や氷量の指標となる。花粉は植生の変化から気候を間接的に推定する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 年輪は空気を保存しないので800,000年は遡れない。有孔虫殻は降雪量を記録しない。花粉はCO2を直接測れない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis (AR6 WG1), Annex VII Glossary, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_AnnexVII.pdf ／ IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.4] The globally averaged sunlight reaching the top of the atmosphere is about one quarter of the solar irradiance measured perpendicular to the Sun's rays at Earth's distance. Why?","h":"球の表面積は断面積の4倍です。","c":["Earth intercepts sunlight over a disk (area pi R squared) but must spread it over the whole sphere (area 4 pi R squared), so the global average is one quarter.","Three quarters of the sunlight is absorbed by the stratosphere before it reaches the top of the atmosphere, so only one quarter of the irradiance remains to be averaged","About 75% of Earth's surface is ocean, which does not receive direct sunlight, so the global average is taken over the one quarter of the surface that is land","The solar irradiance is measured at the Sun's surface, so it decreases by a factor of four before it reaches Earth because the distance to the Sun is four times larger"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 地球は円盤(πR²)で日射を受けるが球全体(4πR²)で平均するため、平均は4分の1になる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 太陽に垂直な面での放射照度（太陽定数、約1361 W/m²）に対し、地球が受ける断面積は円盤πR²、地球表面積は4πR²であり、全球・年平均の入射は約4分の1（約340 W/m²）になる。AR6第7章のエネルギー収支図もこの値を出発点とする。このうち約3割が反射され、残りが吸収される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 成層圏での吸収や海洋面積の割合は4分の1の説明にならない。太陽定数は地球軌道での値で、太陽表面の値ではない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Chapter 7 (The Earth's Energy Budget, Climate Feedbacks and Climate Sensitivity), 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-7/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.4] Which statement best explains the natural greenhouse effect?","h":"短波は通し、長波（赤外線）を吸収・再放射します。","c":["Greenhouse gases reflect incoming sunlight back toward the surface like a mirror, so more of the solar radiation is absorbed by the surface and the lower atmosphere than would otherwise occur, which raises temperature","Greenhouse gases mainly work like a glass roof by blocking convective heat transport away from the surface, rather than by interacting with the infrared radiation emitted by the surface and the atmosphere","Greenhouse gases absorb ultraviolet light in the stratosphere and transfer the heat down to the surface by conduction, which is why the surface is warmer than the equilibrium temperature without them","Greenhouse gases are largely transparent to incoming shortwave solar radiation but absorb and re-emit outgoing longwave (infrared) radiation, including back toward the surface, which raises surface temperature."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 温室効果は、大気が地表からの赤外線を吸収・再放射し、下向きにも戻すことで生じる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 太陽放射（短波）は大気をほぼ通過して地表を温め、地表は赤外線（長波）を放射する。水蒸気・CO2・CH4などはこの赤外線を吸収し、あらゆる方向に再放射するため、地表と下層大気はより高温になる。温室ガラスの比喩は対流の抑制が主因で、地球大気の仕組みとは異なる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「鏡のように反射」「対流を遮る」「紫外線の伝導」はいずれも放射の仕組みを取り違えている。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Chapter 7 (The Earth's Energy Budget, Climate Feedbacks and Climate Sensitivity), 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-7/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.4] The Earth's energy imbalance (absorbed solar radiation minus outgoing longwave radiation) is positive. What does this imply?","h":"正の不均衡は、システムがエネルギーを蓄積し昇温していることを意味します。","c":["The climate system is losing energy and cooling, because more heat is leaving at the top of the atmosphere than is arriving from the Sun over the same period","The climate is in equilibrium, because an imbalance matters only when it is negative, while a positive imbalance is a measurement artefact that averages out over time","The climate system is gaining energy and warming, and this heating is stored mostly in the ocean until outgoing radiation rises enough to restore balance.","Surface temperature must already have reached its long-term equilibrium, so no further warming is committed even if greenhouse gas concentrations stay constant"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 不均衡が正=エネルギー蓄積中。その大半は海洋に入り、まだ平衡に達していない。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.2は、気候システムの加熱率（エネルギー不均衡）が1971〜2006年の0.50 W/m²から2006〜2018年の0.79 W/m²へ増加したと述べる。この正の不均衡は、人為起源の放射強制力（2019年に1750年比で2.72 W/m²）が気候システムを温めていることを反映し、海洋が加熱の91%を吸収している。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「冷却中」「均衡」「平衡到達済み」はいずれも正の不均衡と矛盾する。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.5] According to IPCC AR6 WG3 (2022), which source accounted for the largest share of global net anthropogenic GHG emissions in 2019 (in CO2-equivalent terms)?","h":"約6割を占める最大の排出源です。","c":["Methane (CH4) from all sources combined","Net CO2 from land use, land-use change and forestry","CO2 from fossil fuel combustion and industrial processes","Nitrous oxide (N2O) from fertilizers and other sources"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2019年の最大の排出源は化石燃料・工業由来のCO2（約64%）。次いでCH4（約18%）。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM Figure SPM.1によれば、2019年の世界の人為起源GHG排出は59±6.6 GtCO2eqで、CO2（化石燃料・産業）が約64%、CH4が約18%、土地利用由来の正味CO2が約11%、N2Oが約4%、F-gasが約2%。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CH4は2番目に大きいが約18%。LULUCF由来CO2は約11%、N2Oは約4%と小さい。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.5] Which statement comparing methane (CH4) with CO2 is correct?","h":"寿命は短いがトン当たりの温暖化効果は大きく、評価期間で GWP が変わります。","c":["CH4 persists in the atmosphere for centuries longer than CO2, which is why its GWP is the same for all time horizons and why it dominates long-term warming","CH4 does not absorb infrared radiation directly; its warming effect arises only through the formation of aerosols that trap heat in the lower atmosphere","CH4 has a lower warming effect per tonne than CO2 on every time horizon, but is emitted in far larger quantities, so it still contributes the most to warming","CH4 has a much shorter atmospheric lifetime (about a decade) but a much larger warming effect per tonne, so its GWP is higher over 20 years than over 100 years."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CH4は寿命が約12年と短いがトン当たりの効果が大きく、GWPは評価期間が短いほど大きい。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1第7章は、CH4の大気寿命を約12年とし、GWPは評価期間に依存する（期間が短いほどCH4のGWPは大きい）と評価する。AR6のGWP100は、化石起源CH4で約30、非化石起源で約27。CO2は一部が数百年から数千年の単位で大気中に残る。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CH4が数百年残る・GWPが期間によらず一定・赤外線を吸収しない、は誤り。トン当たりではCH4の方が強い。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Chapter 7 (The Earth's Energy Budget, Climate Feedbacks and Climate Sensitivity), 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/chapter/chapter-7/ ／ IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.5] Which statement about fluorinated gases (HFCs, PFCs, SF6) is correct?","h":"排出量は少ないがGWPが非常に大きい人工ガスです。","c":["They have small emissions and concentrations but very high global warming potentials, and HFCs are being phased down under the Kigali Amendment (2016) to the Montreal Protocol.","They are the largest single contributor to global GHG emissions in CO2-equivalent terms, exceeding CO2 from fossil fuels, which is why they were the first gases phased out under the Paris Agreement","They are produced mainly by natural processes such as wetlands and ruminant livestock, which is why their emissions are not covered by any international phase-down arrangement","The Kigali Amendment, which phases down HFCs, was adopted under the Kyoto Protocol in 2016 and is therefore binding only on the developed countries listed in its Annex B"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> F-gasは少量でもGWPが大きい人工ガス。HFCはモントリオール議定書のキガリ改正で段階削減される。<br><br><b>解説</b> F-gas（HFC・PFC・SF6など）は人工物質で、AR6 WG3 SPMでは2019年排出の約2%と小さいが、GWPは非常に大きい。HFCはオゾン層破壊物質（CFC・HCFC）の代替として普及したが、温室効果が大きいため、2016年のキガリ改正（モントリオール議定書）で段階的削減が合意された。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> F-gasが最大の排出源は誤り（約2%）。自然起源ではなく人工物質。キガリ改正はモントリオール議定書の改正で、京都議定書ではない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本ではフロン排出抑制法とオゾン層保護法の改正（キガリ改正対応）でHFCの規制が進められている。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf ／ UNEP Ozone Secretariat, Kigali Amendment. https://ozone.unep.org/treaties/montreal-protocol/amendments/kigali-amendment-2016-amendment-montreal-protocol-agreed"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.6] IPCC AR6 WG1 assesses the contribution of natural drivers (solar and volcanic) to the change in global surface temperature from 1850-1900 to 2010-2019 as:","h":"自然要因の寄与は小さく、観測された昇温の主因ではありません。","c":["About +0.5°C, explaining roughly half of the observed warming","About -1.0°C, offsetting most of the human-caused warming","Small, in the range of -0.1°C to +0.1°C","Not assessed, because natural drivers cannot be separated from human drivers"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 自然要因（太陽・火山）の寄与は-0.1〜+0.1°Cと小さい。昇温の主因は人為。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.3は、1850〜1900年から2010〜2019年の昇温（最良推定1.07°C）に対し、混合温室効果ガスが+1.0〜2.0°C、エアロゾルなど他の人為要因が0.0〜0.8°Cの冷却、自然要因が-0.1〜+0.1°C、内部変動が-0.2〜+0.2°Cの寄与をしたと評価する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 自然要因を大きな寄与とする選択肢は誤り。寄与の分離は評価済み。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.6] Which of the following human-related emissions exerts a net cooling effect on the climate system?","h":"硫酸塩エアロゾルは太陽光を反射して冷却します。","c":["Carbon dioxide from cement production","Sulphur dioxide, which forms reflective sulphate aerosols","Methane from livestock and rice cultivation","Black carbon deposited on snow and ice"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SO2由来の硫酸塩エアロゾルは正味で冷却。CO2・CH4・雪氷上のブラックカーボンは温暖化。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.3は、エアロゾルなどの人為要因が0.0〜0.8°Cの冷却に寄与し、温室効果ガスの温暖化の一部を覆い隠してきたと述べる。SO2規制で大気汚染が改善すると、この冷却効果が弱まり温暖化が顕在化し得る。ブラックカーボンは日射を吸収し、雪氷面のアルベドも下げるので温暖化側。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ブラックカーボン（煤）は「エアロゾル」でも温暖化要因である点が紛らわしい。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.6] Which statement best explains how deforestation contributes to climate change?","h":"炭素の吸収源を失い、貯蔵炭素をCO2として放出します。","c":["Its only climate effect is a local change in albedo, with no effect on atmospheric CO2, because the carbon in trees is returned directly to the soil at the same site","It releases carbon stored in biomass and soils as CO2 and removes a carbon sink, while also altering surface reflectivity and evapotranspiration.","It affects climate only by increasing aerosol emissions from burning, which always warm the atmosphere, and it has no influence on surface reflectivity or evapotranspiration","It causes warming mainly by depleting the stratospheric ozone layer, which allows additional ultraviolet radiation to reach the surface and heat the land more strongly"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 森林減少はCO2放出と吸収源の喪失に加え、アルベドや蒸発散も変える。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM Figure SPM.1では、土地利用・土地利用変化・林業（LULUCF）の正味CO2が2019年の人為排出の約11%を占める。森林減少は貯蔵炭素の放出と吸収能力の低下に加え、地表の反射率（アルベド）や蒸発散の変化を通じて地域・全球の気候にも影響する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「アルベドのみ」「エアロゾルのみ」「オゾン層破壊が主因」はいずれも誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.7] Which statement about how climate extremes change with additional global warming is consistent with IPCC AR6 WG1?","h":"0.5°Cごとに極端現象がはっきり増える、というのがAR6の評価です。","c":["Changes in extremes become discernible only after the 2°C threshold is crossed; below that, no change in the intensity or frequency of any extreme can be detected in the observational record","Heavy precipitation intensity decreases as the atmosphere warms, because a warmer atmosphere holds less water vapour, and this effect is strongest over the tropical oceans and monsoon regions","Every additional 0.5°C of global warming causes clearly discernible increases in the intensity and frequency of hot extremes and heavy precipitation, and of agricultural and ecological droughts in some regions.","Changes in extremes are uniform across all regions and all types of extreme, so a given amount of global warming produces the same change in heatwaves, droughts and floods everywhere"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 追加の0.5°Cごとに、極端高温・大雨・一部地域の干ばつが明確に増える。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM B.2.2は、地球温暖化が追加で0.5°C進むごとに、熱波を含む極端高温（very likely）と大雨（high confidence）の強度・頻度、および一部地域の農業・生態学的干ばつの明確な増加が生じると述べる。変化は地域・現象で一様ではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「2°Cまで検出不能」「大雨が減る」「一様」は誤り。大気は温暖化で水蒸気を多く保持でき、大雨が強まる。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.7] AR6 WG1 reports warming since 1850-1900 for land and ocean separately (2011-2020). Which is correct?","h":"陸は海より温まりやすく、昇温が大きくなります。","c":["Larger over the ocean (about 1.6°C) than over land (about 0.9°C)","About equal over land and ocean (about 1.1°C each)","Larger over land (about 1.6°C) than over the ocean (about 0.9°C)","Land has cooled slightly while the ocean has warmed by about 1.1°C"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2011〜2020年の昇温は陸域が約1.59°C、海洋が約0.88°C。陸の方が大きい。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.1.2は、世界平均気温が1.09°C上昇し、陸域は1.59 [1.34〜1.83]°C、海洋は0.88 [0.68〜1.01]°Cと、陸域の昇温が大きいと述べる。海洋は熱容量が大きく、蒸発による冷却もあるため昇温が小さい。この空間的な偏りが、地域別の影響の分布に関係する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 陸海を逆にした選択肢が最も紛らわしい。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.7] Which statement about future sea level is consistent with AR6 WG1?","h":"海面上昇は不可逆的で、数世紀〜数千年続きます。","c":["Sea level is committed to rise for centuries to millennia because of continuing deep-ocean warming and ice-sheet melt, and will remain elevated for thousands of years.","Sea level stops rising within a few decades of reaching net-zero CO2 emissions, because the ocean and ice sheets respond to the change in atmospheric forcing almost immediately","Sea level rise is uniform across the globe, with the same increase at every coastline, because ocean water redistributes quickly and land motion plays no role in local relative sea level","Sea level rise is driven only by thermal expansion of seawater; ice-sheet and glacier melt are negligible contributors on the timescales relevant to financial institutions and coastal planners"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 深海の昇温と氷床融解により、海面は数世紀〜数千年にわたり上昇し続ける。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM B.5.4は、海面水位は深海の昇温と氷床の融解により数世紀から数千年にわたって上昇し続け、数千年間高いままであると述べ、今後2000年で温暖化を1.5°Cに抑えても約2〜3 m上昇するとする。過去・将来の排出による変化の多くは数世紀〜数千年不可逆。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「数十年で止まる」「一様」「熱膨張のみ」は誤り。氷河・氷床の融解は主要な寄与。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.8] IPCC AR6 WG2 (2022) estimates how many people live in contexts that are highly vulnerable to climate change?","h":"約33〜36億人です。","c":["Approximately 0.3 to 0.6 billion people","Approximately 3.3 to 3.6 billion people","Approximately 1.0 to 1.5 billion people","More than 7 billion people, the entire world population"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> AR6 WG2は、気候変動に対して脆弱性が高い状況に約33〜36億人が暮らすと評価する。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2 SPM B.2は、約33〜36億人が気候変動に対して非常に脆弱な状況（high vulnerability contexts）に暮らしていると述べる（high confidence）。脆弱性は貧困・ガバナンス・不平等・歴史的な不公正など非気候的要因とも結びつく。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全人口とする選択肢は誇張。数億〜十数億人は過小。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.8] AR6 WG2 compares human mortality from floods, droughts and storms during 2010-2020 between regions of high and very low vulnerability. Mortality in highly vulnerable regions was:","h":"脆弱な地域では桁違いに被害が大きくなります。","c":["About the same","About 2 times higher","About 15 times higher","About 150 times higher"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2010〜2020年、洪水・干ばつ・暴風による死亡率は脆弱性が高い地域で約15倍。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2 SPM B.2.4は、2010〜2020年の洪水・干ばつ・暴風による人的死亡が、脆弱性が非常に低い地域に比べ、脆弱性の高い地域で15倍高かったと述べる。同じハザードでも、脆弱性（社会経済的条件・適応能力）で被害が大きく異なることを示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「ほぼ同じ」は脆弱性の概念と矛盾する。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.8] Which statement about socioeconomic impacts is supported by IPCC AR6 WG2?","h":"農業生産性の伸びは気候変動で鈍化しています。","c":["Climate change has increased agricultural productivity growth in all regions, including the tropics, because higher CO2 and warmer temperatures have uniformly improved yields over the past 50 years","Although overall agricultural productivity has increased, climate change has slowed this growth over the past 50 years globally, with negative impacts mainly in mid- and low-latitude regions.","Observed climate impacts on food and water security are confined to high-income countries, where intensive farming makes crops more sensitive, while low-income regions have seen no measurable effect","Economic damages from climate change have not been detected in any sector, because attribution studies cannot separate climate effects from other drivers of output in agriculture, tourism or energy"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候変動は農業生産性の伸びを鈍化させ、影響は主に中低緯度で顕在化している。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2 SPM B.1.3は、全体の農業生産性は伸びたが、気候変動が過去50年間でその伸びを鈍化させ、負の影響は主に中低緯度、一部の高緯度では正の影響があったと述べる。また農業・林業・漁業・エネルギー・観光などの気候に曝される部門で経済的損害が検出されている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「全地域で生産性が向上」「高所得国に限定」「損害は検出されない」はいずれも評価と逆。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.9] Which description correctly distinguishes transformational adaptation from incremental adaptation?","h":"システムの根本的な属性を変えるのが transformational です。","c":["Transformational adaptation maintains the essence and integrity of a system at a given scale (for example, raising a levee), whereas incremental adaptation changes the fundamental attributes of the system, such as relocating whole settlements","Transformational adaptation means only measures taken after losses have occurred, as a direct response to realised damage, whereas incremental adaptation is always planned in advance and financed by insurance","Transformational adaptation means reducing greenhouse gas emissions at the source, whereas incremental adaptation means reducing exposure to hazards by changing where people live and work in a region","Transformational adaptation changes the fundamental attributes of a system in anticipation of climate change and its impacts (e.g., relocating settlements away from the coast), whereas incremental adaptation maintains the essence and integrity of the system."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> transformationalは根本的な属性を変える適応、incrementalは現状の本質を維持する適応。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2は、transformational adaptationを「気候変動とその影響を見越して社会・生態系システムの根本的な属性を変える適応」と定義する。堤防のかさ上げのように既存システムを維持する対応は漸進的（incremental）適応。適応は緩和（排出削減）とは別概念。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 定義を入れ替えた選択肢が最も紛らわしい。事後対応のみを指すのでも、緩和を指すのでもない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では気候変動適応法（2018年）に基づく気候変動適応計画で適応策を推進している。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.9] A coastal municipality builds a high sea wall that makes shorefront land appear safe, which encourages large new development behind the wall and increases exposure to overtopping events beyond the design standard. This is best described as:","h":"適応策が結果的に曝露や脆弱性を増やす例です。","c":["Transformational adaptation, because it fundamentally changes the coastal system by altering the attributes of the shoreline itself","Effective incremental adaptation with no trade-offs, because the wall reduces the hazard and the new development is therefore fully protected","Maladaptation, because the action increases exposure and may increase the risk of adverse climate-related outcomes","A mitigation measure, because it lowers the greenhouse gas emissions of coastal communities by protecting buildings from flooding"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 適応策が曝露を増やしリスクを高める例はmaladaptation（不適応）。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2は、不適応（maladaptation）を、気候関連の悪影響のリスクを増やす行動（温室効果ガス排出の増加、脆弱性の増加・移転などを含む）と整理する。防潮堤が安全の錯覚を生み、リスクの高い土地利用を促す「堤防効果」は典型例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 壁を築くこと自体は漸進的適応だが、トレードオフがない効果的な適応とは言えない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.9] Which statement correctly describes a 'soft limit' to adaptation, as used by IPCC AR6 WG2?","h":"ソフトな限界は、障壁を解消すれば克服できる限界です。","c":["A limit beyond which no adaptive actions can avoid intolerable risks for the actors or the system concerned, regardless of how much finance or institutional support becomes available later","A limit where adaptation options may exist but are currently not available, mainly because of financial, governance, institutional and policy constraints, and which can be overcome by addressing those constraints.","A limit set by international law on how much adaptation finance a country can receive in a given year from multilateral funds, which can be raised only by amending the relevant treaty text","Any adaptation measure whose cost per tonne of CO2-equivalent avoided is below USD 100, because such measures are considered to face no financial, governance or institutional constraints"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ソフトな限界は、資金・ガバナンス・制度などの制約が原因で、解消すれば克服できる適応の限界。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG2 SPM C.3は、一部の人間系の適応でソフトな限界に達しているが、資金・ガバナンス・制度・政策上の制約への対処で克服できると述べる。一方、ハードな限界は一部の生態系で既に達しており、適応行動では耐えがたいリスクを回避できない状態を指す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「適応行動が存在しない」はハードな限界の説明。USD100/tCO2は緩和コストの目安で適応と無関係。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.10] According to IPCC AR6 WG3 (2022), which options are cited as making large contributions to emission reductions at costs below USD 20 per tCO2-eq by 2030?","h":"コストの低い大きな削減源は、再エネ（太陽光・風力）などです。","c":["Solar and wind energy, energy efficiency improvements, reduced conversion of natural ecosystems, and CH4 emission reductions","Bioenergy with carbon capture and storage (BECCS) and direct air capture, which together provide the largest and cheapest share of the mitigation potential through 2030","Carbon capture and storage applied to fossil power generation, together with nuclear power, which the report identifies as the largest low-cost options for 2030","Nuclear power and offshore wind as the largest low-cost options, together with large-scale afforestation on land that is currently used for agriculture"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> USD20/tCO2未満で大きな削減を生むのは、太陽光・風力、省エネ、自然生態系の転換抑制、CH4削減。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM C.12.1は、USD100/tCO2eq以下の緩和オプションで2030年に世界のGHG排出を2019年水準の少なくとも半分削減でき、USD20未満のオプションはその潜在量の半分超を占め、太陽光・風力、エネルギー効率改善、自然生態系の転換抑制、CH4削減（石炭採掘・石油ガス・廃棄物）がそこで大きな寄与をすると述べる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> BECCS・DAC・化石燃料CCSは高コストで2030年の潜在量も小さい。原子力は低コストの大きな潜在量には挙げられていない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のGX推進戦略（2023年7月閣議決定）に基づく分野別投資戦略でも、水素・アンモニア、再生可能エネルギー等が対象分野に位置づけられている。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.10] Why are sectors such as cement and steel often described as 'hard-to-abate'?","h":"プロセス排出は熱の電化だけでは消せません。","c":["Both sectors emit no fossil-fuel-related CO2 because their energy comes entirely from grid electricity, so no mitigation measures are applicable and decarbonisation depends only on offsetting remaining emissions","Both sectors are exempt from carbon pricing in every jurisdiction, because carbon pricing legislation explicitly excludes heavy industry, which removes any financial incentive to reduce emissions","Their products are not traded internationally, so competitiveness and carbon leakage are not an issue, which means the sectors could decarbonise quickly if only domestic regulation were tightened","A significant share of their emissions are process emissions (e.g., CO2 released when limestone is calcined, or carbon used to reduce iron ore) that cannot be removed simply by electrifying heat."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> セメント・鉄鋼はプロセス排出が大きく、熱源の電化だけでは脱炭素化できない。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3第11章（産業）は、セメントの石灰石の脱炭酸や鉄鋼の還元に伴うプロセス排出が、燃料転換や電化だけでは解決できない課題となることを示す。そのため、素材効率の向上、需要削減、水素還元、CCUSなど複数の手段の組み合わせが議論される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「化石燃料CO2がない」は誤り。「炭素価格が全域で免除」も誤り（EU ETSなどで対象）。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Chapter 11 (Industry), 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/chapter/chapter-11/ ／ IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.10] According to AR6 WG3, which describes the change in unit costs between 2010 and 2019 for solar energy and wind energy?","h":"太陽光が約85%、風力が約55%低下しました。","c":["Solar energy fell by about 55% and wind energy by about 85%","Solar energy fell by about 85% and wind energy by about 55%","Both fell by about 20%","Both rose by about 20% owing to supply chain constraints"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2010〜2019年の単位コストは、太陽光-85%、風力-55%、リチウムイオン電池-85%。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM B.4.1は、2010〜2019年に太陽光（85%）、風力（55%）、リチウムイオン電池（85%）の単位コストが持続的に低下し、導入量が太陽光で10倍超、EVで100倍超増えたと述べる。技術コストの低下は緩和の機会を広げ、課題は系統・蓄電などへ移っている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 太陽光と風力の数字を入れ替えた選択肢が紛らわしい。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.11] Which is a recognized limitation of stratospheric aerosol injection, a solar radiation modification (SRM) approach?","h":"SRMはCO2を減らさないので海洋酸性化は止まりません。","c":["It removes CO2 from the atmosphere and therefore reverses ocean acidification, in addition to cooling the surface by reflecting sunlight in the stratosphere","It is a form of carbon dioxide removal that stores carbon in geological formations, so it reduces the concentration of CO2 in the atmosphere over time","It would not stop atmospheric CO2 concentrations from increasing nor reduce the resulting ocean acidification under continued emissions.","A single injection would lower temperatures for several centuries without repeat deployment, because stratospheric aerosols remain in place for hundreds of years"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SRMは気温を下げ得るがCO2濃度は下げず、海洋酸性化も止められない。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6統合報告書は、SRMは温暖化を1〜2十年で相殺し得るが、CO2濃度の上昇も海洋酸性化も止めないと述べ、新たな広範なリスク、大きな不確実性、ガバナンスの欠如を指摘する。CDR（二酸化炭素除去）とは仕組みが異なる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CO2除去や地層貯留はCDRの説明。エアロゾルは成層圏で数年程度で除去されるため、継続的な投入が必要。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.11] In the context of solar radiation modification, what does 'termination shock' refer to?","h":"SRMを突然やめると、隠れていた温暖化が急に現れます。","c":["A sudden price shock in carbon markets when an emissions trading system is terminated by a government and allowances lose their value overnight","A sudden damage to the ozone layer in the first year after aerosol injection begins, which would immediately reverse the cooling achieved by the injection","The legal consequences that follow when a state withdraws from the Paris Agreement and becomes subject to trade sanctions under the UNFCCC","Rapid climate change that would occur if SRM were suddenly and persistently stopped while greenhouse gas concentrations remain high."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> termination shockは、SRMを急に止めたときに急速な気候変化が生じること。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6統合報告書は、高排出シナリオにおけるSRMの突然かつ持続的な終了は急速な気候変化を引き起こす（high confidence）と述べる。SRMはCO2濃度を下げないため、排出削減と併用せずに依存すると、中止時のリスクが大きい。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素市場の価格ショックやパリ協定離脱は無関係。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 Synthesis Report: Longer Report, 2023. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/syr/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_SYR_LongerReport.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.11] Which is a key drawback associated with deploying bioenergy with carbon capture and storage (BECCS) at the scale assumed in many 1.5°C pathways?","h":"BECCSは大規模では土地と生物多様性への圧力が課題です。","c":["Large-scale bioenergy can put pressure on land and biodiversity, and relies on dependable storage and sustainable biomass supply.","By design it emits more CO2 than coal power with no capture, because the biomass must first be processed using fossil fuels, so it cannot be a source of net removals","It cannot deliver net negative emissions under any circumstances, since the CO2 absorbed by the growing biomass is always released again when the stored carbon leaks from geological storage","It requires injecting reflective aerosols into the stratosphere to work, because the captured carbon must be offset by cooling to keep the biomass crops within their temperature range"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> BECCSは大規模導入で土地・生物多様性への圧力などの課題がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM C.3は、CDRへの依存や、バイオエネルギーに伴う土地・生物多様性への圧力が、資源効率の高い経路や持続可能な発展の経路で大きく軽減されることを述べる。1.5°C経路では2020〜2100年のBECCSによる累積CDRが30〜780 GtCO2とされ、大規模導入の実現可能性が課題となる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> BECCSは理論上、正味でマイナス排出を生み得る。成層圏エアロゾルとは別手法。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.12] Which statement best describes the relationship between cumulative CO2 emissions and global warming that underpins the carbon budget concept?","h":"累積CO2排出量と昇温はほぼ比例します。","c":["Warming is proportional to the annual emission rate, so warming stabilizes as soon as annual emissions stop growing, even if emissions remain at today's high level for decades","There is an approximately linear relationship between cumulative CO2 emissions and global warming, so stabilizing warming requires reaching net-zero CO2 emissions.","Warming reverses immediately when annual emissions are reduced to below the current level, because the concentration of CO2 in the atmosphere responds within a year to any cut","There is no relationship between cumulative emissions and warming, because other forcers such as aerosols and solar variability dominate the global temperature response"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 累積CO2とほぼ線形に昇温するため、気温安定化にはCO2排出の正味ゼロが必要。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM D.1は、人為的なCO2排出による世界平均気温上昇は累積CO2排出量とほぼ線形の関係にあると述べ、気温上昇を特定の水準に抑えるには累積排出量を制限し、少なくともCO2排出を正味ゼロにする必要があると示す。これが炭素予算（残余カーボンバジェット）の根拠。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「年間排出量に比例」「すぐ反転」はいずれも累積の考え方と矛盾する。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.12] AR6 WG1 estimates the remaining carbon budget from the start of 2020 for a 50% likelihood of limiting warming to 1.5°C at about:","h":"約500 GtCO2です。2°Cの数字と混同しないように。","c":["150 GtCO2","500 GtCO2","1,150 GtCO2","2,500 GtCO2"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 1.5°C（50%）の残余カーボンバジェット（2020年初から）は約500 GtCO2。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM Table SPM.2は、2020年初からの残余カーボンバジェットを、1.5°Cに抑える確率50%で500 GtCO2、67%で400 GtCO2、83%で300 GtCO2と示す（2°Cの67%では1,150 GtCO2）。年間約40 GtCO2を排出すると十数年で使い切る規模。AR6以降の更新では数字はさらに小さくなっている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 1,150 GtCO2は2°C・67%の値。150や2,500は桁・水準が合わない。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch1 気候変動の基礎","q":"[LO 1.12] According to IPCC AR6 WG3, global net zero CO2 emissions are reached in which period in modelled pathways limiting warming to 1.5°C (>50%) with no or limited overshoot, and in pathways limiting warming to 2°C (>67%)?","h":"1.5°Cなら2050年代前半、2°Cなら2070年代前半です。","c":["Early 2050s for 1.5°C, and around the early 2070s for 2°C","Early 2040s for 1.5°C, and around the early 2060s for 2°C","Early 2070s for 1.5°C, and around the early 2090s for 2°C","Around 2030 for 1.5°C, and around 2050 for 2°C"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ネットゼロCO2は、1.5°C経路で2050年代前半、2°C経路で2070年代前半。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG3 SPM C.2は、世界のCO2排出が正味ゼロに到達する時期を、1.5°C（>50%、オーバーシュートなし/限定的）で2050年代前半、2°C（>67%）で2070年代前半と示す。1.5°C経路ではGHG排出を2030年に2019年比43%、2050年に84%削減する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 年代をずらした選択肢は、気温目標との対応を取り違えている。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2050年カーボンニュートラルを宣言（2020年10月）し、2025年2月提出のNDCで2035年60%・2040年73%削減（2013年度比）を掲げた。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG3 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGIII_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.1] Which statement reflects the widely cited Brundtland Commission (1987) definition of sustainable development?","h":"将来世代のニーズを損なわない発展です。","c":["Economic growth that maximizes shareholder returns over the next business cycle, with environmental protection left to regulators.","A halt to all economic growth in order to preserve natural resources in their current state.","Development that prioritizes the needs of high-income countries before those of developing countries.","Development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 持続可能な開発は、現在のニーズを満たしつつ将来世代のニーズを損なわない発展。<br><br><b>解説</b> 『Our Common Future』（1987）は、持続可能な開発を「将来の世代が自らのニーズを満たす能力を損なうことなく、現在の世代のニーズを満たす開発」と定義した。重要な概念は、世界の貧困層の不可欠なニーズを最優先に考える「ニーズ」と、技術・社会組織による環境の制約という考え方。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「成長停止」や「株主利益最大化」は定義と矛盾する。先進国優先でもない。<br><br>【出典】World Commission on Environment and Development, Our Common Future (Brundtland Report), 1987. http://www.un-documents.net/ocf-02.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.1] Which set correctly lists the three interdependent and mutually reinforcing pillars of sustainable development recognized by the 2005 UN World Summit Outcome?","h":"経済・社会・環境の3つです。","c":["Economic development, technological development and political stability","Environmental protection, corporate governance and shareholder returns","Social development, military security and energy independence","Economic development, social development and environmental protection"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 3本柱は経済発展・社会発展・環境保護。<br><br><b>解説</b> 2005年の国連首脳会合成果文書（A/RES/60/1）は、持続可能な開発の3つの構成要素として、経済発展、社会発展、環境保護を「相互依存的で相互に補強し合う柱」と位置づけた。ESGのE・S・Gとは別の枠組みで、Gは持続可能な開発の3本柱には含まれない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ガバナンスは3本柱ではない点が紛らわしい。<br><br>【出典】UN General Assembly, 2005 World Summit Outcome (A/RES/60/1), 2005, para. 48. https://documents.un.org/doc/undoc/gen/n05/487/60/pdf/n0548760.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.1] A manufacturer introduces a living-wage policy, supplier labour audits and an occupational safety programme. Which pillar of sustainability do these initiatives primarily address?","h":"賃金・労働安全・サプライヤー監査は社会面です。","c":["Social","Environmental","Economic (resource efficiency)","Governance, which is not part of the three pillars and therefore cannot be assigned"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 生活賃金・労働監査・労働安全は主に社会面（S）の取り組み。<br><br><b>解説</b> 持続可能性の3側面（環境・社会・経済）のうち、従業員・サプライチェーン労働者・地域社会の権利や福祉に関する取り組みは社会面に分類される。環境面は排出・資源・生態系、経済面は事業の長期的な経済価値や雇用・経済発展などを指す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 資源効率は環境・経済面。ガバナンスは3本柱の枠外だが、取り組みの分類を妨げるわけではない（この例は社会面）。<br><br>【出典】UN General Assembly, 2005 World Summit Outcome (A/RES/60/1), 2005, para. 48. https://documents.un.org/doc/undoc/gen/n05/487/60/pdf/n0548760.pdf ／ UN Global Compact, The Ten Principles. https://www.unglobalcompact.org/what-is-gc/mission/principles"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.2] Which statement correctly describes how different entities use sustainability-related frameworks?","h":"CSRは企業の自主的な取り組み、ESGは投資家が評価に使う視点です。","c":["CSR is a legally binding disclosure standard enforced by securities regulators in every major market, whereas ESG is a purely voluntary philanthropic programme run by company foundations and charities","ESG criteria are used only by governments for national policy setting and budget allocation, whereas the SDGs are used only by investors to screen the securities held in their portfolios","Corporate social responsibility (CSR) is a company's self-regulated approach to its social and environmental impacts, while ESG factors are used by investors and analysts to assess a company's material non-financial risks and opportunities.","Sustainable development criteria apply exclusively to financial institutions that take deposits or manage assets, and non-financial companies such as manufacturers or retailers fall outside their scope"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CSRは企業側の自主的な責任の枠組み、ESGは投資家・アナリストが企業を評価する視点。<br><br><b>解説</b> CSRは企業が自社の社会・環境への影響に責任を持つ自主的な枠組みとして発展し、ESGは投資判断で重要となる環境・社会・ガバナンスの要素を評価する枠組みとして用いられる。両者は重なるが、前者は企業の行動、後者は投資家の評価・リスク分析の視点という違いがある。SDGsは政府・企業・金融機関を含む全主体に共通する目標。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> CSRは法的拘束力のある開示基準ではない。ESGは政府専用でも金融機関専用でもない。<br><br>【出典】United Nations, Transforming our world: the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development (A/RES/70/1), 2015. https://sdgs.un.org/2030agenda"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.2] Which statement about ISO 26000 is correct?","h":"ISO 26000は認証用の規格ではなく、ガイダンスです。","c":["It is a certifiable management system standard for which organizations obtain third-party certification.","It sets mandatory quantitative emission-reduction targets for signatory companies.","It applies only to companies listed on stock exchanges.","It provides guidance on social responsibility for organizations of all types, and it is not intended for certification."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ISO 26000は組織の社会的責任に関するガイダンスで、認証を目的としない。<br><br><b>解説</b> ISO 26000:2010は、あらゆる種類・規模の組織を対象とした社会的責任（SR）のガイダンス規格で、ISO 9001や14001のような認証用のマネジメントシステム規格ではない。人権・労働慣行・環境・公正な事業慣行・消費者課題・コミュニティ参画の7つの中核主題を扱う。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 認証対象や上場企業限定、削減目標の義務づけは誤り。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本ではJIS Z 26000がISO 26000に対応している。<br><br>【出典】ISO, ISO 26000 Social responsibility. https://www.iso.org/iso-26000-social-responsibility.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.2] The UN Global Compact asks companies to align with Ten Principles in which four areas?","h":"人権・労働・環境・腐敗防止の4分野です。","c":["Climate, biodiversity, water and waste","Governance, risk, compliance and audit","Production, trade, finance and technology","Human rights, labour, environment and anti-corruption"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 国連グローバル・コンパクトの10原則は、人権・労働・環境・腐敗防止の4分野。<br><br><b>解説</b> 国連グローバル・コンパクトは、企業に人権、労働、環境、腐敗防止の4分野で10原則（人権2、労働4、環境3、腐敗防止1）を事業活動に取り入れるよう求める自主的なイニシアチブで、これらの分野で最低限の基本的責任を果たすことを企業に求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 気候・生物多様性・水・廃棄物は環境分野の一部にすぎない。<br><br>【出典】UN Global Compact, The Ten Principles. https://www.unglobalcompact.org/what-is-gc/mission/principles"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.3] Which statement best describes the relationship between sustainability, ESG and climate change?","h":"気候はEの一要素で、ESGはサステナビリティの一部です。","c":["Climate change is one of the issues within the environmental dimension of ESG, and ESG is a subset (the investment-oriented lens) of the broader concept of sustainability, although climate change also has social and governance implications.","Climate change is treated as a standalone topic outside ESG because it is a scientific issue, whereas ESG covers only governance and social matters such as board structure, executive pay and labour practices","Sustainability is a narrow subset of ESG, and ESG is a narrow subset of climate change, so every sustainability issue can be reduced to a company's greenhouse gas emissions","ESG and sustainability are identical terms used interchangeably by every standard setter, and climate change is excluded from both because it is covered only by treaties between states"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候変動はESGのEの重要要素、ESGはサステナビリティを投資や企業評価に落とし込む枠組み。社会・ガバナンス面にも波及する。<br><br><b>解説</b> サステナビリティは環境・社会・経済を含む広い概念で、ESGはそのうち企業の評価・投資判断に関わる要素を整理した枠組み。気候変動はEに含まれる主要な課題だが、雇用や地域社会への影響（S）、取締役会による監督や報酬連動（G）にも関わる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 気候がESGと無関係とする選択肢、包含関係を逆にした選択肢は誤り。<br><br>【出典】United Nations, Transforming our world: the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development (A/RES/70/1), 2015. https://sdgs.un.org/2030agenda"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.3] Which of the following is typically classified as a governance (G) factor rather than an environmental or social factor?","h":"役員報酬や取締役会の構成はG（ガバナンス）です。","c":["Executive remuneration structure and board independence","Scope 1 greenhouse gas emissions","Employee health and safety record","Water consumption at manufacturing sites"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 役員報酬や取締役会の独立性はG。排出量や水使用はE、労働安全はS。<br><br><b>解説</b> ESGの典型的な分類は、E：排出・エネルギー・水・生物多様性、S：労働条件・安全衛生・人権・地域社会、G：取締役会の構成と独立性、役員報酬、株主の権利、倫理・腐敗防止など。なお、気候関連の報酬連動やボードの気候監督は、気候課題をGに接続する例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> Scope 1排出と水使用はE、労働安全はS。<br><br>【出典】PRI, What are the Principles for Responsible Investment? https://www.unpri.org/about-us/what-are-the-principles-for-responsible-investment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.3] Which statement best illustrates how climate change intersects with all three ESG dimensions?","h":"気候問題はEだけでなく、Sにも、Gにも関わります。","c":["Climate change is purely an environmental matter, so workforce questions and board oversight are unrelated to it, and the S and G pillars only become relevant once a company reports its emissions","Emissions and physical impacts are environmental issues, workforce transition and community effects are social issues, and board oversight of climate risk and climate-linked pay are governance issues.","Climate change affects only the governance dimension, because it is regulated by governments and addressed through disclosure rules, while emissions and community effects fall outside the ESG framework","Climate change affects only the social dimension, because it is caused by human behaviour, while greenhouse gas emissions and physical hazards are not part of the environmental pillar of ESG"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候変動は、排出・物理的影響（E）、労働者・地域への影響（S）、取締役会の監督・報酬連動（G）の全てに関わる。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDはガバナンス（取締役会の監督と経営の役割）を4つの柱の1つに位置づけ、ISSBのIFRS S2も同様の構成を取る。また公正な移行は社会面、排出削減や物理的リスクは環境面に属し、気候課題はESG全体を横断する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「気候はEのみ」「Gのみ」「Sのみ」は一面的で、ESG全体への波及を見落としている。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.4] Which statement about the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) is correct?","h":"17の目標の下に169のターゲットがあります。","c":["The 2030 Agenda sets 8 goals with 21 targets, and applies only to developing countries, which receive the support of developed donors","The SDGs are legally binding treaty obligations with penalties for non-compliance, enforced by the UN General Assembly's review process","The SDGs were adopted in 1992 at the Rio Earth Summit and expired in 2015, when the Millennium Development Goals replaced them","The 2030 Agenda sets 17 goals with 169 targets, and applies to all countries, not only developing countries."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SDGsは17目標・169ターゲット。全ての国に適用される、法的拘束力のない目標。<br><br><b>解説</b> 2015年に国連総会で採択された『持続可能な開発のための2030アジェンダ』は、17の目標と169のターゲットを掲げ、全ての国に普遍的に適用される。法的拘束力はなく、各国が自国の状況に合わせて実施する。8目標・21ターゲットはMDGs（2000年）の構成。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> MDGsとSDGsの混同、法的拘束力の有無が誤答の典型。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本は2016年にSDGs推進本部を設置し、SDGs実施指針を策定している。<br><br>【出典】United Nations, Transforming our world: the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development (A/RES/70/1), 2015. https://sdgs.un.org/2030agenda"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.4] Which SDG number corresponds to 'Climate Action'?","h":"気候変動対策の目標番号です。","c":["SDG 7","SDG 12","SDG 15","SDG 13"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SDG 13が気候変動に具体的な対策を。<br><br><b>解説</b> SDG 13は「気候変動とその影響に立ち向かうため、緊急対策を取る」。SDG 7は「エネルギーをみんなに そしてクリーンに」、SDG 12は「つくる責任 つかう責任」、SDG 15は「陸の豊かさも守ろう」。なお、SDG 13の注記で、気候変動への国際的対応の主要な国際的政府間の場はUNFCCCと認識されている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> SDG 7・12・15も気候関連だが、気候変動そのものはSDG 13。<br><br>【出典】United Nations, Goal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts. https://sdgs.un.org/goals/goal13"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.4] In the SDG Compass guidance for companies, which sequence of five steps is recommended for aligning business strategy with the SDGs?","h":"理解→優先順位→目標設定→統合→報告の順です。","c":["Reporting; setting goals; integrating; defining priorities; understanding the SDGs","Divesting; offsetting; certifying; auditing; litigating","Defining priorities; reporting; understanding the SDGs; integrating; setting goals","Understanding the SDGs; defining priorities; setting goals; integrating; reporting and communicating"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SDG Compassの5ステップは、理解・優先順位づけ・目標設定・統合・報告とコミュニケーション。<br><br><b>解説</b> GRI・国連グローバル・コンパクト・WBCSDが2015年に公表したSDG Compassは、企業がSDGsと整合する戦略を作る5つのステップ（SDGsを理解する、優先課題を定める、目標を設定する、経営に統合する、報告・コミュニケーションする）を示す。SDGsへの整合は、自社事業に関連が深い目標を選び、影響の重要性に基づいて優先順位をつけることで、企業にとって重要（マテリアル）となる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 順序を入れ替えた選択肢は、優先順位づけの前に目標設定や報告をするなど、論理が逆。<br><br>【出典】GRI, UN Global Compact, WBCSD, SDG Compass: The guide for business action on the SDGs, 2015. https://sdgcompass.org/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.5] Which pairing of an ecosystem service with its category (Millennium Ecosystem Assessment) is correct?","h":"木材は供給、洪水調節は調整、レクリエーションは文化サービスです。","c":["Wetlands attenuating floods: regulating service","Timber and fibre: cultural service","Recreation and aesthetic enjoyment: provisioning service","Soil formation and nutrient cycling: provisioning service"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 洪水の緩和は調整サービス。木材は供給、レクリエーションは文化、栄養循環は基盤サービス。<br><br><b>解説</b> ミレニアム生態系評価（2005）は、生態系サービスを供給（食料・水・木材・繊維）、調整（気候・洪水・疾病・水質の調整）、文化（レクリエーション・美的・精神的）、基盤（土壌形成・栄養循環など、他のサービスの前提）の4つに分類した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 木材は供給、レクリエーションは文化、土壌形成は基盤であり、他の組み合わせは分類が入れ替わっている。<br><br>【出典】Millennium Ecosystem Assessment, Ecosystems and Human Well-being: Synthesis, 2005. https://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.356.aspx.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.5] What is the relationship between natural capital and ecosystem services?","h":"自然資本はストック、生態系サービスはそこから流れる便益です。","c":["Ecosystem services are the stock of natural assets such as forests and soils, and natural capital is the flow of benefits that people derive from those assets each year","Natural capital refers only to non-renewable resources such as minerals and fossil fuels, while renewable resources such as forests and fisheries are classified as ecosystem services","Natural capital is the stock of natural assets (e.g., forests, soil, water, air, biodiversity), and ecosystem services are the flows of benefits that people obtain from that stock.","Natural capital and ecosystem services are both man-made capital as defined in national accounts, because their value is recorded only when they are bought and sold in markets"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 自然資本はストック、生態系サービスはそのストックから得られる便益のフロー。<br><br><b>解説</b> 自然資本は、地質・土壌・大気・水・あらゆる生物を含む世界の天然資産のストックで、再生可能・非再生可能の両方を含む。生態系サービスは、それらのストックから人間が得る便益（フロー）。企業は自然資本への依存と影響を評価し、TNFDなどの枠組みで開示する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ストックとフローを入れ替えた選択肢、自然資本を非再生資源に限る選択肢は誤り。<br><br>【出典】Millennium Ecosystem Assessment, Ecosystems and Human Well-being: Synthesis, 2005. https://www.millenniumassessment.org/documents/document.356.aspx.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.5] The World Economic Forum (2020) estimated that what share of global GDP is moderately or highly dependent on nature?","h":"世界GDPの半分超が自然に依存しています。","c":["About 5% (about USD 4 trillion)","About 10% (about USD 9 trillion)","Almost none, since services dominate global output","More than half (about USD 44 trillion)"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> WEFは世界GDPの半分超（約44兆ドル）が自然に中程度以上に依存すると推計した。<br><br><b>解説</b> WEFとPwCの報告書『Nature Risk Rising』（2020）は、世界のGDPの半分を超える約44兆ドルが、自然とその生態系サービスに中程度または高度に依存していると推計した。これは、自然資本の劣化が金融リスクになり得ることの根拠とされる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 5%や10%は過小。サービス業も、食料・水・気候調整などの生態系サービスに間接的に依存する。<br><br>【出典】World Economic Forum and PwC, Nature Risk Rising: Why the Crisis Engulfing Nature Matters for Business and the Economy, 2020. https://www3.weforum.org/docs/WEF_New_Nature_Economy_Report_2020.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.6] Which chronology of key sustainability milestones is correct?","h":"ブルントラント報告(1987)→リオ(1992)→PRI(2006)→パリ協定とSDGs(2015)です。","c":["Rio Earth Summit (1992), Brundtland Report (1987), Paris Agreement (2015), launch of the PRI (2006)","Launch of the PRI (2006), Brundtland Report (1987), SDGs (2015), Rio Earth Summit (1992)","Paris Agreement (2015), Rio Earth Summit (1992), Brundtland Report (1987), launch of the PRI (2006)","Brundtland Report (1987), Rio Earth Summit (1992), launch of the PRI (2006), Paris Agreement and SDGs (2015)"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ブルントラント(1987)→リオ地球サミット(1992)→PRI(2006)→パリ協定・SDGs(2015)。<br><br><b>解説</b> ブルントラント委員会報告（1987）が持続可能な開発を定義し、1992年のリオ地球サミットでUNFCCC・生物多様性条約が署名開放され、2006年にPRIが開始、2015年にSDGsとパリ協定が採択された。ESGという用語は2004年の国連グローバル・コンパクト『Who Cares Wins』で普及した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 順序を入れ替えた選択肢は、PRIやパリ協定をブルントラントやリオより前に置くなど時系列が誤り。<br><br>【出典】World Commission on Environment and Development, Our Common Future (Brundtland Report), 1987. http://www.un-documents.net/ocf-02.htm ／ PRI, What are the Principles for Responsible Investment? https://www.unpri.org/about-us/what-are-the-principles-for-responsible-investment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.6] Which initiative is generally credited with popularizing the term 'ESG' in the financial industry in 2004?","h":"国連グローバル・コンパクトの報告書です。","c":["The Kyoto Protocol (1997)","The UN Global Compact report 'Who Cares Wins' (2004)","The TCFD Recommendations (2017)","The EU Taxonomy Regulation (2020)"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ESGという用語は、2004年の国連グローバル・コンパクト『Who Cares Wins』で広まった。<br><br><b>解説</b> 国連グローバル・コンパクトが金融機関と共同で2004年に公表した『Who Cares Wins』は、環境・社会・ガバナンスの課題を資産運用や証券分析に統合することを提唱し、ESGという用語を普及させた。この流れが2006年のPRIにつながる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 京都議定書・TCFD・EUタクソノミーはいずれもESGという語の起源ではなく、時期も異なる。<br><br>【出典】UN Global Compact, Who Cares Wins: Connecting Financial Markets to a Changing World, 2004. https://www.unglobalcompact.org/library/1"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.6] Which statement about the TCFD and its successor arrangements is correct?","h":"TCFDの役割は2023年にISSBへ引き継がれました。","c":["The TCFD was created by the IPCC and published its final recommendations in 1997, and its monitoring role was later taken over by the UNFCCC secretariat in 2015","The TCFD was created by the Financial Stability Board, published final recommendations in 2017, and its monitoring role was taken over by the IFRS Foundation (ISSB) in 2023.","The TCFD was created by the European Commission, and its recommendations are legally binding in all G20 countries, where they are enforced by national securities regulators","The TCFD was created by the UN Global Compact in 2004 and still monitors company disclosures today, publishing an annual status report on the use of its recommendations"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TCFDは金融安定理事会(FSB)が設置し、2017年に最終提言。2023年に役割はISSBへ移った。<br><br><b>解説</b> FSBがG20の要請を受けて2015年にTCFDを設置し、2017年に気候関連財務情報開示の最終提言を公表した。2023年にTCFDは役割を終えて解散し、企業の気候関連開示のモニタリングはIFRS財団（ISSB）が引き継いだ。IFRS S2はTCFD提言の内容を取り込んでいる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> IPCCや欧州委員会が設置したのではない。TCFD提言自体に法的拘束力はない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のTCFD賛同機関は2023年11月時点で1,488機関に達した（経済産業省）。また、SSBJ基準（2025年3月公表）はISSB基準（IFRS S1・S2）との整合を基本方針としている。<br><br>【出典】FSB, Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures. https://www.fsb-tcfd.org/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.7] A company labels its product 'eco-friendly' without explaining what environmental benefit it provides or providing evidence. Which problem is most directly illustrated?","h":"根拠のない漠然とした環境表示は、グリーンウォッシュの典型です。","c":["A vague, generic environmental claim that is not substantiated, of the type restricted by EU consumer-protection rules","A fully compliant claim, because 'eco-friendly' is a term defined by ISO 14040 and may be used on any product that has completed a life cycle assessment","A disclosure required under the GHG Protocol Scope 3 standard, which obliges every company selling consumer goods to label products as eco-friendly","A carbon offset claim that has been verified by a third-party registry, which allows the company to use any environmental descriptor on its products"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 『eco-friendly』のような根拠のない曖昧な環境主張は、グリーンウォッシュの典型。<br><br><b>解説</b> EUの指令(EU) 2024/825は、『environmentally friendly』『eco-friendly』『green』『climate friendly』などの包括的な環境主張を、認められた優れた環境性能の裏づけなしに行うことを禁じる。英国CMAのGreen Claims Codeも、主張は明確で曖昧でなく、立証できる必要があるとする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ISO 14040はLCAの規格で、『eco-friendly』を定義していない。検証済みオフセットの話ではない。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本では、景品表示法の優良誤認表示（消費者庁）が環境主張にも適用され得る。<br><br>【出典】European Union, Directive (EU) 2024/825 empowering consumers for the green transition, 2024. https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/825/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.7] Which practice is known as 'greenhushing'?","h":"取り組みをあえて公表しないことです。","c":["Overstating a product's environmental benefits in advertising or on its packaging so that consumers believe the product is greener than the evidence shows","Purchasing carbon credits to offset all of a company's Scope 1 emissions and then describing the company in public communications as carbon neutral","Publishing a sustainability report according to the GRI Standards without obtaining any assurance, so that readers cannot rely on its contents at all","Deliberately under-communicating or concealing a company's sustainability targets or progress to avoid scrutiny or criticism"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> グリーンハッシングは、批判を避けるため、環境の取り組みや目標をあえて公表しないこと。<br><br><b>解説</b> グリーンウォッシュが環境主張の誇張なのに対し、グリーンハッシングは、訴訟・規制・批判を恐れて取り組みを公に語らない行動。この結果、市場が実際の取り組みを評価できず、投資家の意思決定を妨げ得る。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 広告での誇張はグリーンウォッシュ。オフセット購入やGRI報告そのものは対象外。<br><br>【出典】European Union, Directive (EU) 2024/825. https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/825/oj ／ UK CMA, Green Claims Code, 2021. https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/green-claims-code-making-environmental-claims"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.7] Under EU Directive (EU) 2024/825, which claim is among the practices banned in consumer communications?","h":"オフセットに基づく中立表示が禁止されます。","c":["Stating the product's measured energy consumption per use on its label, in a form that allows consumers to compare it with similar products","Publishing an independently verified product carbon footprint with a clearly disclosed methodology and the underlying life-cycle data","Claiming that a product has a neutral, reduced or positive impact on greenhouse gas emissions based on offsetting","Disclosing a company's SBTi-validated emission reduction targets in its annual report, together with the progress made against the targets"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 指令2024/825は、オフセットに基づき『GHGへの影響が中立・削減・プラス』と主張することを禁じる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 指令(EU) 2024/825は、事業者が、製品が温室効果ガス排出に与える影響が中立・削減・プラスであるとの主張を、排出量クレジットのオフセットに基づいて行うことを不公正な取引慣行として禁止する。加盟国は2026年3月27日までに国内法化し、2026年9月27日から適用する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 測定値の表示、検証済みフットプリント、SBTi目標の開示は禁止対象ではない。<br><br>【出典】European Union, Directive (EU) 2024/825. https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/825/oj"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.8] Which sequence correctly lists the four phases of life-cycle assessment under ISO 14040/14044?","h":"目的と範囲→インベントリ→影響評価→解釈の4段階です。","c":["Interpretation; life-cycle inventory; certification by a third-party verifier; and reporting of the results to the public","Goal and scope definition; impact assessment; inventory analysis; and carbon offsetting of the remaining emissions","Scope 1 accounting; Scope 2 accounting; Scope 3 accounting; and independent verification of the reported totals","Goal and scope definition; life-cycle inventory analysis; life-cycle impact assessment; interpretation"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> LCAは、目的と範囲の設定、インベントリ分析、影響評価、解釈の4段階。<br><br><b>解説</b> ISO 14040/14044は、LCAを、目的及び調査範囲の設定、ライフサイクルインベントリ分析（LCI）、ライフサイクル影響評価（LCIA）、ライフサイクル解釈の4つの相に整理する。解釈は各段階と反復的に行われ、結果を意思決定に役立てる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 並べ替えや、Scope 1〜3の会計とは別物。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本ではJIS Q 14040/14044がLCAを規定する。<br><br>【出典】ISO, ISO 14040:2006 Environmental management - Life cycle assessment - Principles and framework. https://www.iso.org/standard/37456.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.8] In an LCA, what is the 'functional unit'?","h":"比較の基準となる単位です。","c":["A quantified description of the function of the product system, used as a reference unit so that environmental impacts can be compared on an equivalent basis","The total weight of all raw materials used by the company in a given reporting year, which is the reference unit to which all inventory flows in the study are scaled","The legal entity that is responsible for commissioning the LCA report and that must sign the critical review statement required by the standard for every study","The monetary value of the product at the point of sale, which is used as the reference unit so that environmental impacts can be compared per dollar of revenue"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 機能単位は、製品システムの機能を定量化した基準単位。<br><br><b>解説</b> 機能単位は、比較可能性を確保するため、製品システムが提供する機能を定量的に定義したもの（例：『1年間、100 m²の床を洗浄する』『1,000 kmを移動する』）。LCAの目的と範囲の設定で決める。製品の重量や価格そのものではなく、提供する機能を基準にする。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原材料総重量、報告主体、販売価格は機能単位ではない。<br><br>【出典】ISO, ISO 14040:2006. https://www.iso.org/standard/37456.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.8] What does a 'cradle-to-gate' LCA boundary include?","h":"原料採取から工場出荷までで、使用と廃棄は含みません。","c":["Raw material extraction through production, use and end-of-life disposal, including recycling of the product at the end of its service life","Raw material extraction through production up to the factory gate, excluding the use and end-of-life phases","Only the use phase of the product, including the energy and consumables needed during operation but not production or disposal","Only the transport of the finished product from the factory gate to the retailer, excluding all upstream and downstream stages"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> cradle-to-gateは、原料採取から工場出荷まで。使用と廃棄は含まない。<br><br><b>解説</b> LCAのシステム境界の代表は、cradle-to-gate（ゆりかごから出荷まで）とcradle-to-grave（ゆりかごから墓場まで）。前者は使用段階と廃棄段階を含まない。後者は使用・廃棄を含むため、製品全体の環境影響を把握でき、企業はこれでホットスポットを特定してサステナビリティを高める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 使用・廃棄を含むのはcradle-to-grave。<br><br>【出典】ISO, ISO 14040:2006. https://www.iso.org/standard/37456.html"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.9] Which statement correctly contrasts the target audiences of major sustainability reporting frameworks?","h":"ISSBは投資家向け、GRIは広いステークホルダー向けです。","c":["The GRI Standards are designed exclusively for investors and lenders and focus only on financial materiality, whereas the ISSB Standards are designed for the general public, NGOs and civil society groups","Both the ISSB and GRI Standards are designed only for financial regulators and prudential supervisors, and neither is intended for investors, employees, communities or other stakeholders of the reporting company","The ISSB Standards (IFRS S1 and S2) are designed to meet the information needs of investors and other capital market participants, whereas the GRI Standards are designed for a broad range of stakeholders and focus on an organization's impacts.","The ISSB Standards address only social and human-capital issues, whereas the GRI Standards address only climate-related matters, so companies must apply the two frameworks in separate reports"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> ISSBは投資家向けの財務マテリアリティ、GRIは多様なステークホルダー向けのインパクト報告。<br><br><b>解説</b> ISSB基準（IFRS S1・S2）は、投資家など資本市場の参加者に有用なサステナビリティ関連財務情報を提供することを目的とする。GRIスタンダードは、組織が経済・環境・人に与える影響を、幅広いステークホルダー向けに報告するための基準。EUのESRSは両方の視点（ダブルマテリアリティ）を求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 対象読者を入れ替えた選択肢は誤り。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のSSBJ基準はISSB基準に対応している。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation, IFRS S1 General Requirements for Disclosure of Sustainability-related Financial Information, 2023. https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/ifrs-s1-general-requirements/ ／ GRI, GRI Standards. https://www.globalreporting.org/standards/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.9] Which statement about the SASB Standards is correct?","h":"77業種に分かれた業種別基準で、今はISSBの下にあります。","c":["They are industry-specific standards covering 77 industries, and are now maintained by the ISSB under the IFRS Foundation.","They are a single cross-industry standard that does not distinguish between industries, and they apply a common list of metrics to every reporting company","They are issued by the European Commission as part of the CSRD and are mandatory for all large companies established in EU member states","They apply only to financial institutions such as banks and insurers and exclude all other sectors, which are covered by separate sector standards"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> SASB基準は77業種別で、現在はIFRS財団(ISSB)の下で維持されている。<br><br><b>解説</b> SASB基準は、SICS（Sustainable Industry Classification System）に基づく77業種ごとに、財務的に重要なサステナビリティ課題と指標を示す。2022年にSASBはIFRS財団に統合され、ISSBはIFRS S1の適用にあたってSASB基準を参照するよう求めている。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 単一基準・EU委員会発行・金融機関限定は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IFRS Foundation / SASB, SASB Standards. https://sasb.ifrs.org/standards/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.9] What is CDP?","h":"投資家などの要請で企業に環境情報の開示を求める仕組みです。","c":["A government agency established under the Paris Agreement that sets mandatory carbon taxes and collects them from companies, cities and regions in proportion to their reported emissions","A non-profit disclosure system through which companies, cities and regions report environmental data (such as climate, forests and water) using an annual questionnaire, often at the request of investors and customers","A credit-rating agency that rates the creditworthiness of sovereign and corporate debt, and uses climate data submitted by issuers to adjust the ratings it publishes each year","An accounting standard setter that issues the financial reporting standards used in audited statements, including rules on how companies must recognise carbon liabilities"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> CDPは、企業などが気候・森林・水の環境情報を質問書で開示する非営利の仕組み。<br><br><b>解説</b> CDP（旧Carbon Disclosure Project）は、投資家や調達企業の要請を受け、企業・自治体が気候変動・森林・水セキュリティの環境情報を年次の質問書で開示する国際的な非営利の開示システム。企業の開示内容は評価（スコア）され、投資家などが利用する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 政府機関でも、格付機関でも、会計基準設定主体でもない。<br><br>【出典】CDP, About us. https://www.cdp.net/en/info/about-us"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.10] A bank adopts an impact-analysis process and sets and publishes targets in at least two areas where it has its most significant impact. Which Principle for Responsible Banking is primarily being implemented?","h":"インパクトの特定と目標設定は原則2です。","c":["Principle 2: Impact and Target Setting","Principle 1: Alignment","Principle 4: Stakeholders","Principle 6: Transparency and Accountability"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> インパクト分析と目標設定は、責任銀行原則の原則2。<br><br><b>解説</b> 責任銀行原則（PRB、2019年）の6原則は、1 整合性（Alignment）、2 インパクトと目標設定（Impact & Target Setting）、3 顧客（Clients & Customers）、4 ステークホルダー、5 ガバナンスと企業文化、6 透明性と説明責任。原則2は、銀行が自らの最も重大なポジティブ・ネガティブ・インパクトを分析し、少なくとも2つの分野で目標を設定して公表することを求める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原則1は戦略をSDGs・パリ協定に整合させること、原則4はステークホルダーとの協働、原則6は開示と自己評価。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.10] A bank's board establishes oversight of its sustainability commitments and links remuneration to the achievement of responsible-banking goals. Which Principle for Responsible Banking is primarily being implemented?","h":"経営陣のガバナンスと企業文化は原則5です。","c":["Principle 3: Clients and Customers","Principle 2: Impact and Target Setting","Principle 5: Governance and Culture","Principle 4: Stakeholders"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 取締役会の監督と報酬連動は、原則5（ガバナンスと企業文化）。<br><br><b>解説</b> 原則5は、銀行が実効性のあるガバナンスと責任ある銀行業の文化を通じて原則へのコミットメントを実行することを求める。サステナビリティ目標の取締役会による監督、経営陣の責任の明確化、従業員の理解と報酬への反映が代表的な施策。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原則3は顧客の持続可能な慣行の奨励、原則4は関係者との協働、原則2は目標設定。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.10] A bank works with its corporate clients to encourage sustainable practices and develop products and services that create shared prosperity. Which Principle for Responsible Banking is primarily being implemented?","h":"顧客との協働は原則3です。","c":["Principle 1: Alignment","Principle 3: Clients and Customers","Principle 5: Governance and Culture","Principle 6: Transparency and Accountability"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 顧客との協働による持続可能な慣行の奨励は、原則3。<br><br><b>解説</b> 原則3（顧客）は、銀行が顧客・取引先と協働し、持続可能な慣行を奨励して、現在・将来の世代に共通の繁栄をもたらす経済活動を可能にすることを求める。移行計画の策定支援やサステナブル商品の提供などが例。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原則1は自行戦略の整合、原則5は社内のガバナンス、原則6は開示。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.11] In the UNEP FI approach to impact analysis for banks, how are a bank's areas of most significant impact generally identified?","h":"ポートフォリオの規模と、国・地域のニーズに照らした影響の大きさで決めます。","c":["By selecting the three business lines with the highest revenue, irrespective of the nature of their impacts or the needs of the countries and regions where the bank operates","By choosing only those areas where the bank has no measurable impact, so that no targets are needed and the public reporting requirement can be met with a short statement","By copying the target areas chosen by the largest competitor in the same market, so that the bank's disclosures remain comparable across the peer group and supervisors can benchmark them","By combining the scale of the bank's exposure in each sector or product with the relevance of the impacts to the needs of the countries or regions where it operates"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最も重大なインパクトは、ポートフォリオの規模と、事業地域のニーズに対する関連性で特定する。<br><br><b>解説</b> PRBの影響分析では、銀行がまずポートフォリオの範囲（スコープ）を定め、業種・商品ごとの事業規模と、事業を行う国・地域の課題（ニーズ）に照らした影響の重要性を組み合わせて、最も重大なインパクト領域を特定する。そのうえで、パフォーマンスを測定し、目標を設定する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 収益上位の事業を選ぶ方法や、競合の模倣は影響分析ではない。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.11] Which target is most consistent with the Principles for Responsible Banking requirement that targets be specific, measurable and time-bound?","h":"基準年・期限・数値のある目標が条件に合います。","c":["Improve our contribution to a sustainable future in the coming years by working closely with clients, stakeholders and our employees","Do our best to support clients in the energy transition wherever commercially feasible, and report on progress whenever we are able to","Reduce the financed emissions of our power-generation portfolio by 40% by 2030, relative to a 2020 baseline","Be recognized as a leader in sustainable finance among regional banks and enhance our reputation with customers and rating agencies"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 基準年・数値・期限がある目標が、SMARTな目標の例。<br><br><b>解説</b> PRBは、銀行が自行の最も重大なインパクト領域で、SMART（具体的・測定可能・達成可能・関連性がある・期限がある）な目標を設定して公表することを求める。『2030年までに2020年比40%削減』のように基準年・数値・期限が明確な目標が適切。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「今後数年で改善」「最善を尽くす」「リーダーになる」は、数値・期限がなく測定できない。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.11] Which statement about public reporting under the Principles for Responsible Banking is correct?","h":"ポジティブ・ネガティブ両方のインパクトを透明に開示します。","c":["Signatory banks must disclose only their positive impacts, because negative impacts are treated as confidential supervisory information that may be shared with regulators but not with the general public","Signatory banks commit to be transparent about, and accountable for, their positive and negative impacts and their contribution to society's goals, by periodically reviewing implementation and publicly reporting on progress.","Signatory banks are exempt from any public reporting during the first ten years of membership, after which they must publish a single report that covers the whole period in aggregate form","Public reporting is the responsibility of UNEP FI rather than of individual banks, which publishes one consolidated progress report on behalf of all signatories and requires no bank-level disclosures"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> PRB署名銀行は、正負両方のインパクトについて透明性と説明責任を負い、進捗を公表する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 原則6は、銀行が原則の実施状況を定期的に見直し、ポジティブ・ネガティブ両方のインパクトと社会目標への貢献について透明性を持ち、説明責任を果たすことを求める。署名銀行は、PRBの報告・自己評価の枠組みに沿って、進捗を公に報告する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ポジティブな面のみの開示、10年間の免除、UNEP FIによる代行はいずれも誤り。<br><br>【出典】UNEP FI, Principles for Responsible Banking. https://www.unepfi.org/banking/bankingprinciples/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.12] Which of the following is NOT one of the six Principles for Responsible Investment (PRI)?","h":"PRIは化石燃料企業の一律除外を求めていません。","c":["We will incorporate ESG issues into investment analysis and decision-making processes.","We will be active owners and incorporate ESG issues into our ownership policies and practices.","We will exclude all fossil fuel companies from every portfolio.","We will report on our activities and progress towards implementing the Principles."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> PRIの6原則に『化石燃料企業の一律除外』はない。<br><br><b>解説</b> PRIの6原則は、1 ESG課題を投資分析・意思決定に組み込む、2 積極的な株主としてESGを所有方針・慣行に組み込む、3 投資先にESGの適切な開示を求める、4 業界での原則の受容と実施を促進する、5 実効性を高めるために協働する、6 活動と進捗を報告する。特定業種の一律除外は含まれない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つはいずれもPRIの原則そのもの。<br><br>【出典】PRI, What are the Principles for Responsible Investment? https://www.unpri.org/about-us/what-are-the-principles-for-responsible-investment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.12] An asset manager votes its shares in line with a climate policy and engages with portfolio companies on emissions targets. Which PRI principle is primarily being implemented?","h":"議決権行使とエンゲージメントは原則2です。","c":["Principle 1: incorporating ESG issues into investment analysis","Principle 2: being active owners","Principle 4: promoting acceptance of the Principles in the industry","Principle 6: reporting on activities and progress"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 議決権行使とエンゲージメントは原則2（積極的な株主）。<br><br><b>解説</b> PRI原則2は、投資家が積極的な株主として、ESG課題を所有方針や慣行に組み込むことを求める。議決権行使、投資先との対話（エンゲージメント）、株主提案などが代表的な手段。原則1は投資分析・意思決定への統合。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原則1は分析段階、原則4は業界全体への働きかけ、原則6は報告。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本ではスチュワードシップ・コードも、投資家による建設的な対話を求めている。<br><br>【出典】PRI, What are the Principles for Responsible Investment? https://www.unpri.org/about-us/what-are-the-principles-for-responsible-investment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch2 サステナビリティ","q":"[LO 2.12] A group of institutional investors joins a collaborative engagement initiative to jointly press large emitters to improve climate governance and disclosure. Which PRI principle does this best illustrate?","h":"投資家同士の協働は原則5です。","c":["Principle 5: working together to enhance effectiveness","Principle 1: incorporating ESG issues into investment analysis","Principle 3: seeking appropriate disclosure on ESG issues by entities invested in","Principle 6: reporting on activities and progress"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 投資家同士の協働エンゲージメントは原則5（協働して実効性を高める）。<br><br><b>解説</b> PRI原則5は、署名機関が原則の実施の実効性を高めるために協働することを求める。共同エンゲージメントのイニシアチブへの参加はその典型的な方法。原則3は投資先に開示を求めることで、協働の有無を問わない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 原則3が最も紛らわしいが、問われているのは『投資家同士が協働する』点。<br><br>【出典】PRI, What are the Principles for Responsible Investment? https://www.unpri.org/about-us/what-are-the-principles-for-responsible-investment"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.1] A bank's commercial real-estate loans are secured by coastal properties. A severe flood damages several of the properties. Through which traditional financial risk channel is this physical risk most directly transmitted to the bank?","h":"担保価値の低下と借り手の返済力の低下は信用リスクです。","c":["Market risk, because the properties are traded on a regulated exchange","Liquidity risk, because the bank is unable to meet depositor withdrawals on that day","Credit risk, through lower collateral values and weaker borrower repayment capacity","Strategic risk, which is the only risk category affected by physical hazards"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 物理的リスクは担保価値の低下や借り手の返済力低下を通じて、主に信用リスクに波及する。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル銀行監督委員会（BCBS 2021）は、物理的リスク・移行リスクというリスクドライバーが、信用リスク・市場リスク・流動性リスク・オペレーショナルリスクといった既存のリスク区分に波及すると整理した。洪水による担保物件の損傷は、担保価値の低下（LGD上昇）と借り手の収益減（PD上昇）を通じて信用リスクを高める。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 市場リスクは市場価格の変動、流動性リスクは資金繰り。物理的ハザードは「戦略リスクだけ」には限定されない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.1] A government introduces a substantial carbon tax. A power-utility borrower relying on coal cannot pass the cost on to customers, and its margins fall sharply. What is the most direct effect for its lender?","h":"借り手の収益悪化は、デフォルト確率の上昇につながります。","c":["Higher credit risk, because the borrower's profitability and debt-service capacity deteriorate (a higher probability of default)","Lower credit risk, because the carbon tax increases the borrower's cash inflows by raising electricity prices for every producer in the market","No effect on the lender, because transition risk applies only to equity investors, while a lender's claims rank ahead of shareholders and are unaffected","A direct operational loss to the lender, caused by a failure of its own internal processes, people or systems in handling the borrower's account"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素税による借り手の収益悪化は、貸し手のデフォルト確率の上昇（信用リスク）として現れる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクは、政策・技術・市場・評判の変化が企業の収益・資産価値に与える影響を通じて、財務リスクに転換する。炭素税で費用が増え、価格転嫁もできない場合、借り手の返済能力が低下し、貸し手のPDが上がる。同じ要因は株価（市場リスク）にも影響する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「移行リスクは株主だけの問題」は誤り。融資にも影響する。オペレーショナルリスクの定義は内部プロセス等の失敗。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.1] According to the Basel Committee's analysis of climate-related risk drivers, how should climate-related risk be viewed in relation to traditional risk categories?","h":"新しいリスク種ではなく、既存のリスクを増幅するドライバーです。","c":["Climate-related risk is a distinct fifth risk category that is entirely independent of credit, market, liquidity and operational risk, and it therefore needs its own separate Pillar 1 capital charge","Climate-related risk affects only operational risk, because the main risk drivers are physical events such as floods and storms that damage a bank's own premises, branches and data centres","Climate-related risk affects financial institutions only when they hold fossil fuel assets directly on their balance sheets, so banks with no such holdings can disregard the Basel analysis","Climate-related risks are drivers that act through, and can be captured within, existing risk categories such as credit, market, liquidity and operational risk, rather than a separate standalone risk type."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候関連リスクは、既存リスク区分に波及するリスクドライバー。独立したリスク種ではない。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS（2021）の報告書は、物理的リスク・移行リスクを気候関連のリスクドライバーとし、マクロ・ミクロの波及経路を通じて、信用・市場・流動性・オペレーショナルなどの伝統的なリスクを高め得ると整理した。気候リスクをこれらの既存の枠組みの中で識別・測定・管理する考え方の根拠になる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「独立した第5のリスク」「オペレーショナルのみ」「化石燃料資産に限る」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.2] Two factories face the same flood hazard. Factory A is on a floodplain, and Factory B is on high ground. Which element of the risk framework (hazard, exposure, vulnerability) explains the difference in expected loss?","h":"同じハザードでも立地の違いは曝露の違いです。","c":["Hazard, because the two factories experience different climate drivers","Exposure, because Factory A has assets located where the hazard occurs","Vulnerability, because Factory B has no assets that could be damaged","Mitigation, because Factory A emits more greenhouse gases"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 同じハザードで損失が違う原因が立地（ハザードにさらされる資産の有無）なら、曝露（exposure）の違い。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCC AR6 WG2は、気候関連リスクを、気候ハザード・曝露・脆弱性の動的な相互作用から生じるものとして整理する。曝露は、ハザードの影響を受け得る場所にある人・資産の存在。同じハザードでも、氾濫原にある工場は曝露が大きい。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 問題文はハザードが同じと述べている。Factory Bにも資産はあるが、そもそも曝露が小さい。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.2] Two coastal hotels have identical exposure to the same storm surge. Hotel A has flood barriers, backup power and business-interruption insurance, while Hotel B has none. What explains the difference in expected loss?","h":"備えの有無による影響の受けやすさは、脆弱性の違いです。","c":["Hazard, because Hotel A faces a weaker storm","Exposure, because Hotel B has more guests","Vulnerability, because Hotel A is better able to cope with and absorb the impact","Transition risk, because Hotel A has lower carbon emissions"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 同じ曝露でも、防護・備え・保険の有無による差は脆弱性（vulnerability）の違い。<br><br><b>解説</b> IPCCの枠組みでは、脆弱性は、悪影響を受けやすい性質で、感度（影響の受けやすさ）や対処・適応能力を含む。防潮設備、非常用電源、保険は損失を抑える（脆弱性を下げる）。曝露とハザードは同一なので、残る要素は脆弱性。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> ハザードや曝露は同一と設定されている。移行リスクは別の概念。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG2 Summary for Policymakers, 2022. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg2/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGII_SummaryForPolicymakers.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.2] In applying the hazard-exposure-vulnerability logic to transition risk, which example best represents 'vulnerability'?","h":"排出が多い（曝露）だけでなく、対応できるかどうかが脆弱性です。","c":["A newly introduced carbon price, which is the policy driver that raises costs for emitters across the whole economy and acts on every company","A company's high Scope 1 emissions, which represent the asset base exposed to the policy and determine how much carbon cost it will have to pay","A company's limited ability to pass carbon costs through to customers or to switch to low-carbon technology","A national climate law that is passed by parliament and sets the sectoral emission caps, which is the driver rather than a company-level characteristic"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 移行リスクでは、コスト転嫁や技術転換ができない程度が脆弱性。ドライバーは政策・技術、曝露は排出集約的な資産。<br><br><b>解説</b> 移行リスクでは、ドライバー（政策・技術・市場・評判の変化）、曝露（炭素集約的な資産・事業）、脆弱性（その変化に対応できる能力の低さ）に分けて整理できる。炭素価格がかかっても、価格転嫁や低炭素技術への転換ができる企業は脆弱性が低い。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素価格・法律はドライバー、高い排出は曝露に当たる。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.3] According to McGlade and Ekins (Nature, 2015), what share of global fossil fuel reserves would need to remain unused between 2010 and 2050 to have a reasonable chance of limiting warming to 2°C?","h":"石炭は8割超、ガスは約半分、石油は約3分の1です。","c":["About 5% of oil, 5% of gas and 5% of coal reserves","About 90% of oil reserves, but no gas or coal reserves","About one third of oil reserves, about half of gas reserves and over 80% of coal reserves","None; all proven reserves can be used under a 2°C pathway if carbon capture is not used"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 2°C目標には、石油の約3分の1、ガスの約半分、石炭の8割超が未使用のまま残る必要がある。<br><br><b>解説</b> McGlade & Ekins（2015）は、2010〜2050年に2°C目標と整合するには、世界の確認埋蔵量のうち石油の約33%、天然ガスの約49%、石炭の82%超を使わずに残す必要があると推計した。これが座礁資産（stranded assets）リスクの根拠の1つ。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 5%という少量や、「全て使用可能」は結論と逆。石炭が最も大きく制約される。<br><br>【出典】McGlade, C. and Ekins, P., The geographical distribution of fossil fuels unused when limiting global warming to 2°C, Nature 517, 187-190, 2015. https://www.nature.com/articles/nature14016"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.3] Which asset is most clearly exposed to stranding risk from regulation on building energy performance?","h":"最低エネルギー性能基準を満たさない建物は賃貸できなくなるおそれがあります。","c":["An offshore wind farm with a long-term power purchase agreement that guarantees a fixed price for its output, which makes it the asset most exposed to building-energy regulation","A solar farm connected to the grid under a feed-in tariff, since a tightening of minimum energy performance standards for buildings would prevent the farm from selling electricity","A newly built building certified to the highest energy performance class, since stricter standards are applied retroactively and require such buildings to be rebuilt every decade","A commercial building that does not meet a minimum energy performance standard and cannot legally be let without costly retrofits"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 最低エネルギー性能基準を満たさない建物は、規制により賃貸・売却ができず座礁資産化し得る。<br><br><b>解説</b> 座礁資産は、予期せぬ早期の評価減・価値低下・負債化に見舞われる資産。規制（最低エネルギー性能基準、炭素価格、化石燃料車の禁止など）、技術、市場、物理的リスクが要因となり、不動産、化石燃料、火力発電、内燃機関車などが対象となる。再エネ発電は逆に移行の恩恵を受ける。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 再エネ発電所や高性能建築物は、移行によって価値が高まる側。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.3] Which of the following is an example of an asset stranded by a physical (rather than transition) climate risk?","h":"洪水や海面上昇で使えなくなる資産は物理的リスク由来です。","c":["A coal-fired power plant closed early because of a new carbon price","A coastal resort that becomes uninsurable and uninhabitable because of repeated storm-surge flooding","Oil reserves that cannot be sold because of declining demand for oil","A petrol-vehicle production line made obsolete by a ban on new internal-combustion-engine sales"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 洪水・海面上昇で保険がかけられず使えなくなる資産は、物理的リスクによる座礁。<br><br><b>解説</b> 座礁資産は移行リスクだけでなく、物理的リスクでも生じる。繰り返す高潮・洪水で保険不能・居住不能になった沿岸リゾートは物理的リスク由来。炭素価格、需要減、販売禁止は移行リスク（政策・市場）由来。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つはいずれも政策・市場に起因する移行リスク。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.4] Which pair consists only of chronic physical risks?","h":"慢性リスクは、長期的な気候パターンの変化です。","c":["Tropical cyclones and flash floods","Wildfires and hailstorms","Rising mean temperatures and sea-level rise","Heatwave events and river floods"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 平均気温の上昇と海面上昇は慢性リスク。台風・洪水・山火事は急性リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDは物理的リスクを、急性（サイクロン・洪水など極端現象の頻度・深刻度の増加）と慢性（降水パターンの変化、気温の上昇、海面上昇など長期的な気候パターンの変化）に分類する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 台風・フラッシュフラッド・山火事・ひょう・熱波・河川洪水はイベント型の急性。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.4] A vineyard is destroyed by a wildfire in a single week. Over the following decades, shifts in average temperature and rainfall also make the region unsuitable for the same grape varieties. Which classification is correct?","h":"1週間の山火事は急性、数十年の気候パターン変化は慢性です。","c":["The wildfire is an acute hazard, and the long-term shift in climate suitability is a chronic hazard.","Both are chronic hazards because they relate to climate, and neither should be treated as an event-driven acute hazard","The wildfire is a chronic hazard, and the long-term shift in suitability is an acute hazard, because fires last longer than climatic shifts","Both are transition risks because they affect agricultural companies, which are exposed to policy change rather than climate hazards"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 山火事は急性ハザード、長期の気温・降水の変化は慢性ハザード。<br><br><b>解説</b> 急性・慢性の区別は、現象の継続期間と性質による。単発のイベント（山火事、洪水、暴風）は急性、長期的に進行する平均気温の上昇や降水パターンの変化は慢性。どちらも物理的リスクで、移行リスクではない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「両方とも慢性」「分類が逆」「両方とも移行リスク」はいずれも誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.4] Which statement about acute and chronic physical hazards is correct?","h":"慢性ハザードは徐々に進み、急性はイベント的に発生します。","c":["Chronic hazards occur suddenly and last only a few days, while acute hazards develop gradually over decades, such as a progressive change in mean temperature or rainfall patterns","Chronic hazards develop gradually over long periods (e.g., sea-level rise), while acute hazards are event-driven (e.g., cyclones), and acute events can occur on top of the chronic trend.","Chronic hazards are always less costly than acute hazards, because slow-onset changes give firms time to adapt, so financial institutions can safely ignore them in credit analysis","Acute hazards cannot be linked to climate change, only chronic hazards can, because individual extreme events always arise from natural variability and have no connection to long-term warming"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 慢性は徐々に進行する長期的変化、急性は突発的なイベント。慢性の上に急性が重なる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 海面上昇（慢性）は高潮（急性）の被害を大きくするように、慢性と急性は重なって損失を増やす。AR6 WG1は、人為起源の気候変動が熱波・大雨・干ばつ・熱帯低気圧などの極端現象にすでに影響していると評価する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 定義の逆転、「慢性は常に低コスト」、「急性は気候変動と無関係」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf ／ IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.5] Which statement about the sources of uncertainty in climate projections (Hawkins and Sutton, 2009) is correct?","h":"近い将来は内部変動、遠い将来はシナリオの不確実性が大きくなります。","c":["Scenario uncertainty dominates at all horizons, including the next five years, so near-term projections depend almost entirely on which emissions pathway is assumed by the modeller","Internal variability becomes the dominant source of uncertainty for end-of-century global mean temperature, because natural fluctuations grow with the length of the projection and overwhelm the forced signal","For near-term projections, internal variability is relatively more important, while for end-of-century global temperature, scenario (emissions pathway) uncertainty becomes the dominant source.","Model uncertainty is negligible at every horizon because all climate models agree closely on the climate response, so projections differ only through the emissions scenario chosen"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 近い将来は内部変動、世紀末はシナリオ（排出経路）の不確実性が主要因となる。<br><br><b>解説</b> Hawkins & Sutton（2009）は、気候予測の不確実性を、内部変動、モデルの不確実性、シナリオの不確実性に分けた。短い時間スケールでは内部変動の相対的重要性が高く、世紀末の全球平均気温ではシナリオ不確実性が支配的になる。リスク管理上は、複数シナリオでの評価が必要という含意がある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 全期間でシナリオが支配的、世紀末に内部変動が支配的、モデル不確実性が無視できる、は誤り。<br><br>【出典】Hawkins, E. and Sutton, R., The potential to narrow uncertainty in regional climate predictions, Bulletin of the American Meteorological Society 90(8), 2009. https://journals.ametsoc.org/view/journals/bams/90/8/2009bams2607_1.xml"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.5] Which statement about the accuracy of hazard-model predictions for physical risk is most appropriate?","h":"粗い解像度では、局地的な極端現象を直接表現しにくいです。","c":["Global climate models have coarse grid resolution, so local extremes (for example, convective rainfall and flash floods) are not directly resolved, and downscaling and bias correction add further uncertainty.","Global climate models resolve every individual building and drainage channel, so asset-level predictions of flood and wind damage are exact once the emissions scenario has been chosen by the analyst","Hazard-model accuracy is essentially identical for temperature, precipitation and tropical cyclones, so a single validation exercise is enough to establish confidence in every hazard in a portfolio","Because projections contain uncertainty, hazard models should not be used in risk assessment at all, and supervisors expect banks to rely only on historical loss records for physical risk"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 全球気候モデルは解像度が粗く、局地的な極端現象は直接表現できない。ダウンスケールにも不確実性が伴う。<br><br><b>解説</b> 気温など大規模な変数に比べ、降水・熱帯低気圧・洪水などの局地的な現象は予測精度が低い。ダウンスケーリングで細かい情報を得ても、元モデルや補正手法の不確実性は残る。不確実性があっても、幅を認識した上でシナリオ分析に使うのが標準的な考え方。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「正確」「精度は同じ」「使うべきでない」は不適切。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.5] AR6 WG1 assesses the equilibrium climate sensitivity (ECS), a key source of model uncertainty. Which is correct?","h":"最良推定値は3°C、非常に可能性が高い範囲は2〜5°Cです。","c":["The best estimate is 1°C, and the very likely range is 0.5°C to 1.5°C.","The best estimate is 6°C, and the very likely range is 5°C to 8°C.","The best estimate is 3°C, and the very likely range is 2°C to 5°C.","ECS has no best estimate because it cannot be assessed."],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> AR6のECS最良推定値は3°C、非常に可能性が高い範囲は2〜5°C（可能性が高い範囲は2.5〜4°C）。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1 SPM A.4.4は、複数の証拠に基づき、ECSの最良推定値を3°C、可能性が高い（likely）範囲を2.5〜4°C、非常に可能性が高い（very likely）範囲を2°C（高信頼度）〜5°C（中程度の信頼度）とする。AR5には最良推定値がなく、1.5〜4.5°Cだった。範囲が広いことは、将来リスクの評価で不確実性を考慮する必要性を示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の範囲は評価と異なる。AR6は最良推定値を示した。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.6] Which is a major data challenge when modelling the direct physical risk of a loan portfolio?","h":"借入人の本社所在地と実際の資産の所在地は異なることが多いです。","c":["Hazard data are not needed, because the asset locations alone determine all physical risk, and any given location has the same exposure to flood, heat, wind and drought hazards","Precise geographic locations of the borrowers' assets are often unavailable, since a company's registered address is not the location of its facilities.","All asset-level data are available in standardised public registers, including facility coordinates, construction type and protection measures, so the challenge lies only in processing time","Physical-risk data are always forward-looking and require no assumptions about emissions scenarios, downscaling or model selection, since they come directly from observed local measurements"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 借入人の資産の正確な所在地データが不足している（本社住所≠施設の所在地）。<br><br><b>解説</b> NGFSは、物理的リスク評価のデータ課題として、資産の位置情報（ジオコーディング）の欠如、損害関数（ハザードと被害額の関係）の不足、ハザードデータの粒度、サプライチェーンの可視性不足を挙げる。ハザード別の情報も必要。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「資産の所在地だけで決まる」「標準化された公的登録簿がある」は誤り。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Final report on bridging data gaps, 2022. https://www.ngfs.net/en/final-report-bridging-data-gaps"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.6] Why are damage (vulnerability) functions a data challenge for modelling direct physical risk?","h":"ハザードの強さと被害額の関係は、建物の構造などに依存します。","c":["Damage functions are unnecessary because hazard intensity alone determines the financial loss, regardless of the construction type, elevation, protection measures or occupancy of the exposed asset","Damage functions are identical across all asset types and regions, so a single curve calibrated on one country can be applied to every property in a loan portfolio without adjustment","Damage functions are available for every asset and are updated daily by public agencies, so the only remaining difficulty is the cost of storing the very large quantity of data","The relationship between hazard intensity and financial damage depends on asset characteristics (such as building type, elevation and protection measures) that are rarely available in financial data."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 損害関数は、建物の種類・標高・防護の有無など、金融データでは得にくい資産特性に依存する。<br><br><b>解説</b> 洪水の浸水深が同じでも、建物の構造、階数、防護設備、事業継続計画によって損害額は変わる。損害関数の構築には資産ごとの詳細な属性が必要だが、金融機関は通常そのデータを持たない。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 損害は「ハザードの強さだけ」「全資産で同一」では決まらない。<br><br>【出典】NGFS, Final report on bridging data gaps, 2022. https://www.ngfs.net/en/final-report-bridging-data-gaps"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.6] Which time-horizon issue complicates physical-risk modelling for financial institutions?","h":"融資期間と気候の変化が顕在化する期間にずれがあります。","c":["Climate scenarios cover only the next 12 months, which is longer than any loan maturity, so a bank's physical-risk models always capture the full period over which scenarios diverge","Loans typically mature after 2100, so the horizon mismatch is irrelevant, and short-term risk metrics always fully capture the long-term differences between climate scenarios in a bank's portfolio","Loan and investment horizons (often 5 to 10 years) are shorter than the horizon over which climate signals diverge between scenarios (2050 and beyond), so short-term risk metrics may not capture the longer-term risk.","Physical-risk projections cannot be extended beyond the current year, so financial institutions can only assess risks over a one-year horizon and must ignore longer-dated exposures altogether"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 金融機関の融資期間は短く、気候シナリオの差が出る期間（2050年以降）との間にずれがある。<br><br><b>解説</b> AR6 WG1が示すように、シナリオ間の温度差は2040年代以降に拡大する。金融機関の与信期間は通常それより短く、短期の信用リスク指標だけでは長期のリスクを捉えにくい。一方で、不動産の担保価値など、将来のリスクを織り込んで今の価格が変わる経路もある。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> シナリオが12か月のみ、満期が2100年以降、という前提は誤り。<br><br>【出典】IPCC, AR6 WG1 Summary for Policymakers, 2021. https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg1/downloads/report/IPCC_AR6_WGI_SPM.pdf ／ NGFS, Final report on bridging data gaps, 2022. https://www.ngfs.net/en/final-report-bridging-data-gaps"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.7] A manufacturer's own plants are not flooded, but a key supplier's factory is closed for months because of flooding. Which type of climate-related risk does this illustrate?","h":"自社が被災していなくても、サプライヤー経由で影響が及びます。","c":["Direct physical risk, because the manufacturer owns the affected factory","Indirect physical risk, through supply chain disruption","Transition risk, because floods are caused by policy changes","Litigation risk, because the supplier will necessarily be sued"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> サプライヤーの被災による調達途絶は、間接的な物理的リスク（サプライチェーン経由）の例。<br><br><b>解説</b> 直接的な物理的リスクは自社資産の損傷。間接的な物理的リスクは、サプライチェーンの寸断、原材料価格の高騰、取引先や顧客の被災、保険の利用可能性や価格の変化、マクロ経済への影響など、自社が直接被災しなくても生じる影響。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 自社所有の工場が被災した場合は直接リスク。洪水は政策ではなく物理的ハザード。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm ／ TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.7] Insurers raise premiums sharply or withdraw coverage for properties in a high-flood-risk area, and property values in that area fall. Which type of risk does this best illustrate?","h":"保険の撤退や保険料の上昇を通じた資産価値の下落は間接リスクです。","c":["Transition risk caused by a carbon tax","Direct physical risk to the insurers' own buildings only","Indirect physical risk, through changes in insurance availability and asset values","Operational risk caused by errors in the insurers' internal systems"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 保険の撤退・保険料の上昇による資産価値の下落は、間接的な物理的リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理的リスクの伝播経路には、保険の利用可能性・コストの変化がある。保険を付けられない地域では、住宅ローン・不動産担保の価値が下がり、銀行の信用リスクに波及する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素税は移行リスク。保険会社の内部システムの誤りはオペレーショナルリスク。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.7] Which statement best describes how physical climate hazards can create macro-level indirect risk for banks?","h":"ソブリンの財政悪化が、国債保有や貸出に波及します。","c":["Climate shocks affect only the physical assets of households and firms, and never the macroeconomy, so banks face no channel from physical hazards to sovereign risk or to system-wide credit conditions","Climate shocks can weaken a country's output and fiscal position, which can pressure sovereign creditworthiness and, via banks' sovereign holdings and loans, transmit to the financial system.","Sovereign credit risk is unrelated to climate hazards by definition, because governments can always raise taxes or print money, so bank sovereign holdings are insulated from physical climate shocks","Macro-level effects arise only from transition policies such as carbon taxes, never from physical hazards, because physical events are local and cannot change output or fiscal positions nationally"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 気候ショックは国の生産・財政を弱め、ソブリンの信用力や銀行の保有国債・貸出を通じて金融システムへ波及し得る。<br><br><b>解説</b> BCBS（2021）は、気候関連リスクドライバーが、ミクロ（個別企業・家計）とマクロ（経済全体）の波及経路を通じて銀行に影響し得ると整理する。マクロ経路には、生産性の低下、資源価格の変化、ソブリンリスク、金融市場の変動が含まれる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 物理的ハザードはマクロ経済にも影響する。移行政策だけが原因とするのは誤り。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Climate-related risk drivers and their transmission channels, April 2021. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d517.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.8] According to the TCFD, which is a category of climate-related opportunity?","h":"TCFDの機会は5分類（資源効率、エネルギー源、製品・サービス、市場、レジリエンス）です。","c":["Reputation risk","Resource efficiency","Litigation exposure","Stranded assets"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> TCFDの機会の分類は、資源効率、エネルギー源、製品・サービス、市場、レジリエンス。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDは気候関連の機会を、資源効率、エネルギー源、製品・サービス、市場、レジリエンスの5分野に分類する。評判リスク、訴訟、座礁資産はいずれもリスク側の概念。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 評判・訴訟は移行リスクの分類（政策・法、技術、市場、評判）、座礁資産もリスク。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.8] A company diversifies its supply chain and develops adaptation measures to withstand more frequent extreme weather. Under the TCFD categories, which type of opportunity is this?","h":"供給網の多様化と適応による耐性の向上はレジリエンスです。","c":["Resilience","Energy source","Products and services","Resource efficiency"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 調達の多様化や適応策による耐性強化は、TCFDの『レジリエンス』の機会。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDの機会のうち、レジリエンスには、再生可能エネルギープログラムへの参加や省エネの導入、資源の代替・多様化が含まれ、気候変動に伴うリスクへの耐性を高めることで、競争優位や安定した事業運営につなげる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> エネルギー源は低排出エネルギー源への転換、製品・サービスは新製品開発、資源効率は効率的な生産・輸送。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.8] Which is an example of an opportunity arising from physical climate risk?","h":"物理的リスクの高まりは、適応関連の製品・サービスの需要を生みます。","c":["Increased demand for flood defences, drought-resistant crops and climate-resilient infrastructure","Higher costs from carbon taxes on a coal producer, which reduce its margins and make its remaining reserves less valuable","Writing down coal reserves because of lower demand for thermal coal, which reduces the book value of mining assets","Litigation against a company for misleading environmental claims, which creates legal costs and reputational harm for it"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 洪水対策・耐干ばつ作物・強靭なインフラの需要拡大は、物理的リスクに伴う機会。<br><br><b>解説</b> 物理的リスクが高まると、適応製品・サービス（防災設備、耐性のある作物、保険商品、建設・エンジニアリング）の需要が増える。TCFDは、製品・サービス、市場、レジリエンスの機会を示す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 炭素税のコスト・石炭の評価減・訴訟は、いずれも移行リスクのコスト側。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.9] A battery manufacturer's cost declines make electric vehicles cheaper than petrol vehicles, reducing demand for an engine maker's products. Under the TCFD classification, which transition risk driver is this?","h":"既存製品が低排出技術に置き換わるのは技術リスクです。","c":["Policy and legal risk","Reputation risk","Acute physical risk","Technology risk"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 既存製品が低排出技術に置き換わる動きは、技術リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDは移行リスクを、政策・法、技術、市場、評判の4つに分類する。技術リスクは、既存の製品・サービスの低排出の代替品による置き換えや、新技術への投資の失敗などを含む。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 政策・法は規制・訴訟、評判は利害関係者の見方の変化。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.9] Customers increasingly switch to lower-carbon alternatives, and raw-material prices change in response to climate-related shifts in supply and demand. Under the TCFD classification, which transition risk driver is this?","h":"顧客行動の変化や原材料価格の変動は市場リスクです。","c":["Market risk","Technology risk","Policy and legal risk","Chronic physical risk"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 顧客行動の変化や原材料価格の変動は、市場リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDの市場リスクは、顧客行動の変化、市場シグナルの不確実性、原材料コストの上昇を含む。技術リスクは新技術への置き換え、政策・法リスクは規制や訴訟。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 技術リスクと混同しやすいが、問われているのは需要・価格の動き。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.9] Which of the following is classified as a policy and legal transition risk by the TCFD?","h":"排出報告義務の強化・訴訟は政策・法のリスクです。","c":["Substitution of existing products with lower-emission options","Enhanced emissions-reporting obligations and exposure to climate-related litigation","Shifts in consumer preferences","Increased stakeholder concern or negative stakeholder feedback"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 排出報告義務の強化や訴訟リスクは、政策・法リスク。<br><br><b>解説</b> TCFDの政策・法リスクには、GHG排出価格の上昇、排出報告義務の強化、既存製品・サービスへの義務化と規制、訴訟への曝露が含まれる。製品の代替は技術、消費者選好は市場、ステークホルダーの懸念は評判のリスク。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つはそれぞれ、技術・市場・評判の例。<br><br><b>日本との対応</b> 日本のSSBJ基準（2025年3月公表）は、ISSB基準と整合する形で気候関連開示を定める。<br><br>【出典】TCFD, Recommendations of the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures, 2017. https://assets.bbhub.io/company/sites/60/2020/10/FINAL-2017-TCFD-Report-11052018.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.10] Which statement best describes human capital as a potential 'stranded asset' in the low-carbon transition?","h":"特定産業に特化した技能は、その産業が縮小すると価値を失います。","c":["Human capital cannot be affected by the transition, since workers' skills are general and are not tied to any industry, so no retraining or income support is ever required","Human capital is stranded only when workers retire, because skills never lose value while a person remains employed, regardless of whether the employer's industry is in decline","Human capital is a financial asset that appears on the balance sheet as a fixed asset, and its stranding is recorded as an impairment charge whenever a plant closes","Workers' skills tied to declining carbon-intensive industries may lose value, and affected workers and communities may face job losses, which raises just-transition challenges."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 縮小する炭素集約産業に特化した技能は価値を失い得る。雇用と地域への影響が公正な移行の課題となる。<br><br><b>解説</b> 座礁資産は設備や埋蔵量だけでなく、特定産業に結びついた人的資本にも当てはまる。石炭産業などの労働者は、転職や再教育が必要となり、地域経済も影響を受ける。公正な移行は、そうした影響を最小限に抑え、質の高い雇用を創出することを目指す。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 技能が産業に無関係とする選択肢、退職時のみ座礁とする選択肢は誤り。人的資本は貸借対照表の固定資産ではない。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, Paris Agreement, 2015, Preamble. https://unfccc.int/sites/default/files/english_paris_agreement.pdf"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.10] Which international text refers to 'the imperatives of a just transition of the workforce and the creation of decent work and quality jobs'?","h":"パリ協定の前文です。","c":["The Kyoto Protocol (1997)","The Montreal Protocol (1987)","The Basel III framework (2017)","The Preamble of the Paris Agreement (2015)"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 『労働力の公正な移行』『ディーセント・ワークと質の高い雇用』に言及するのは、パリ協定の前文。<br><br><b>解説</b> パリ協定（2015）の前文は、国内で定められた開発の優先事項に従い、労働力の公正な移行とディーセント・ワークおよび質の高い雇用の創出が不可欠であることを考慮すると述べる。ILOは2015年に公正な移行のガイドラインを策定した。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 京都議定書・モントリオール議定書・バーゼルIIIは労働力の公正な移行に言及する文書ではない。<br><br>【出典】UNFCCC, Paris Agreement, 2015, Preamble. https://unfccc.int/sites/default/files/english_paris_agreement.pdf ／ ILO, Guidelines for a just transition towards environmentally sustainable economies and societies for all, 2015. https://www.ilo.org/publications/guidelines-just-transition-towards-environmentally-sustainable-economies"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.10] Which is a typical challenge associated with delivering a just transition?","h":"雇用の減少は特定の地域に集中しやすいです。","c":["Job losses are spread evenly across all regions and sectors, so no targeted support is needed, and general unemployment benefits are sufficient to address the effects of phasing out coal","A just transition requires halting all emissions reductions until no jobs are affected, since protecting existing employment is the first and overriding objective of climate policy","Job losses from phasing out carbon-intensive activities are often geographically concentrated, so affected communities need retraining, alternative employment and social protection.","Workers in carbon-intensive industries can always move to new jobs without retraining, because the skills used in fossil-fuel activities transfer directly to every low-carbon sector"],"a":2,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 炭素集約産業の雇用減少は特定地域に集中しやすく、再教育・代替雇用・社会的保護が必要。<br><br><b>解説</b> ILOの公正な移行のガイドラインは、環境面で持続可能な経済への移行を、すべての人にとって公正で包摂的なものにすることを求め、社会対話、技能開発、社会的保護、雇用政策などを柱とする。炭鉱町のように、産業と地域が結びついている場合、影響は集中する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 雇用減少が全国一様に分散する、排出削減を止めるべき、再教育が不要、はいずれも誤り。<br><br>【出典】ILO, Guidelines for a just transition. https://www.ilo.org/publications/guidelines-just-transition-towards-environmentally-sustainable-economies"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.11] Under the Basel Framework, how is operational risk defined?","h":"内部プロセス・人・システムの不備、外部事象による損失で、法務リスクを含み戦略・評判リスクを除きます。","c":["The risk of loss from adverse movements in market prices, such as interest rates, exchange rates, equity prices and commodity prices, on positions held in the trading book and banking book","The risk that a counterparty fails to meet its contractual obligations in full when due, including both the borrower's default and the deterioration of its credit quality over a loan's life","The risk that a bank cannot meet its payment obligations as they fall due without incurring unacceptable losses, even when funding markets are under stress for several weeks","The risk of loss resulting from inadequate or failed internal processes, people and systems or from external events, including legal risk but excluding strategic and reputational risk."],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> オペレーショナルリスクは、内部プロセス・人・システムの不備や外部事象による損失で、法務リスクを含み、戦略・評判リスクは含まない。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル枠組み（OPE10）はオペレーショナルリスクを、不適切または機能しない内部プロセス・人・システム、または外部事象から生じる損失のリスクと定義し、法務リスクを含み、戦略リスクと評判リスクを除く。市場リスクは市場価格の変動、信用リスクは取引相手の債務不履行、流動性リスクは支払い義務の履行不能。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 他の3つは、市場・信用・流動性リスクの定義。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel Framework, OPE10 Definition of operational risk and loss. https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/chapter/OPE/10.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.11] Which three risk categories are covered by the minimum capital requirements under Pillar 1 of the Basel framework?","h":"第1の柱は信用・市場・オペレーショナルの3つです。","c":["Credit risk, liquidity risk and reputational risk","Credit risk, market risk and operational risk","Market risk, strategic risk and legal risk","Operational risk, liquidity risk and climate risk"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> バーゼルの第1の柱（最低所要自己資本）は、信用リスク・市場リスク・オペレーショナルリスクを対象とする。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル枠組みの第1の柱は、信用リスク、市場リスク、オペレーショナルリスクに対する最低所要自己資本を定める。流動性リスクは自己資本ではなく、流動性カバレッジ比率（LCR）や安定調達比率（NSFR）で規律される。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 流動性リスクや評判・戦略リスクは第1の柱の自己資本の対象ではない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel Framework. https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.11] A bank holds a bond denominated in a foreign currency without hedging, and the exchange rate moves against the bank. Which major financial risk category does the resulting loss fall under?","h":"為替の変動による損失は市場リスクです。","c":["Credit risk","Liquidity risk","Operational risk","Market risk (foreign exchange risk)"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 為替レートの不利な変動による損失は、市場リスク（為替リスク）。<br><br><b>解説</b> 市場リスクは、金利、為替、株価、商品価格などの市場価格の不利な変動によって生じる損失のリスク。債券の発行体が債務不履行になる場合は信用リスク、資金繰りの問題は流動性リスク、内部プロセスの失敗は運営上のリスク。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 為替損失は取引相手の不履行ではない。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel Framework. https://www.bis.org/basel_framework/"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.12] A bank estimates a corporate loan with a probability of default (PD) of 2%, loss given default (LGD) of 40% and exposure at default (EAD) of USD 1,000,000. What is the expected loss?","h":"期待損失=PD×LGD×EADです。","c":["USD 20,000","USD 400,000","USD 800","USD 8,000"],"a":3,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> 期待損失 = PD × LGD × EAD = 2% × 40% × 1,000,000 = 8,000ドル。<br><br><b>解説</b> 信用リスクの計測では、期待損失（EL）をPD（デフォルト確率）、LGD（デフォルト時損失率）、EAD（デフォルト時エクスポージャー）の積で計算する。0.02 × 0.40 × 1,000,000 = 8,000。気候リスクはPDやLGDを通じてこの式に反映できる。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 20,000はPD×EAD、400,000はLGD×EAD、800は桁を誤った値。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, An Explanatory Note on the Basel II IRB Risk Weight Functions, 2005. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/irbriskweight.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.12] Which statement about the shift in the Basel market-risk framework (Fundamental Review of the Trading Book) is correct?","h":"VaR（99%）から期待ショートフォール（97.5%）へ移行しました。","c":["Expected shortfall at a 97.5% confidence level replaces value-at-risk at a 99% confidence level for internal models.","Value-at-risk at a 99.9% confidence level replaces expected shortfall for internal models, because regulators found expected shortfall too sensitive to tail events","Market-risk capital is removed from Pillar 1 and moved to Pillar 2, so that banks set the capital charge for trading positions through supervisory review alone","Market risk is measured only by the number of trades booked in the trading book over a quarter, with a fixed capital charge applied to each trade"],"a":0,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> FRTBでは、内部モデルの99%VaRに代わり、97.5%の期待ショートフォール（ES）を用いる。<br><br><b>解説</b> バーゼル委員会の「市場リスクの最低所要自己資本」（2019年改訂）は、内部モデル方式のVaR（99%）を、テール損失をより捉えやすい期待ショートフォール（97.5%）に置き換えた。市場リスクは、VaRやESなどの統計的手法でリスク量を測り、限度枠で管理する。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 「99.9%VaR」「第1の柱から除外」「取引数で測定」はいずれも誤り。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Minimum capital requirements for market risk, January 2019. https://www.bis.org/bcbs/publ/d457.htm"},
  {"f":"SCR:Ch3 気候リスク","q":"[LO 3.12] Which description of the Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR) is correct?","h":"ストレス下の30日間の純資金流出に耐える高品質流動資産を求めます。","c":["Banks must hold capital equal to 8% of total assets, regardless of how liquid those assets are, so that the ratio rises mechanically whenever the bank lends more to its customers","Banks must hold high-quality liquid assets at least equal to total net cash outflows over a 30-calendar-day stress period (a ratio of at least 100%).","Banks must fund all long-term assets with equity only, so that no maturity transformation takes place and a run by short-term depositors cannot affect the bank's solvency position","Banks must hold liquid assets equal to the expected losses on their loans over the next year, calculated as the sum of PD times LGD times EAD across all exposures"],"a":1,"v":"primary","n":"<b>ひとことで</b> LCRは、30日間のストレス期間の純資金流出に対し、高品質流動資産（HQLA）を100%以上確保する規制。<br><br><b>解説</b> 流動性リスクの管理では、LCR（ストレス下の30日間の純資金流出をHQLAで賄う）と、1年の安定調達の観点を持つNSFRを使う。いずれもバーゼルIIIで導入された流動性規制。<br><br><b>紛らわしい選択肢</b> 自己資本比率や期待損失とは別の概念。<br><br>【出典】BCBS, Basel III: The Liquidity Coverage Ratio and liquidity risk monitoring tools, 2013. https://www.bis.org/publ/bcbs238.htm"}
];
